basic-resource-type;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/basic-resource-type;4.0.1;BasicResourceTypes;Basic Resource Types;draft;False;This value set defines codes for resources not yet supported by (or which will never be supported by) FHIR.  Many of the codes listed here will eventually be turned into official resources.  However, there is no guarantee that any particular resource will be created nor that the scope will be exactly as defined by the codes presented here.  Codes in this set will be deprecated if/when formal resources are defined that encompass these concepts.;;FHIR Project team;complete;advevent;Adverse Event;An undesired reaction caused by exposure to some agent (e.g. a medication, immunization, food, or environmental agent).;;;
basic-resource-type;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/basic-resource-type;4.0.1;BasicResourceTypes;Basic Resource Types;draft;False;This value set defines codes for resources not yet supported by (or which will never be supported by) FHIR.  Many of the codes listed here will eventually be turned into official resources.  However, there is no guarantee that any particular resource will be created nor that the scope will be exactly as defined by the codes presented here.  Codes in this set will be deprecated if/when formal resources are defined that encompass these concepts.;;FHIR Project team;complete;aptmtreq;Appointment Request;A request that a time be scheduled for a type of service for a specified patient, potentially subject to other constraints;;;
