contact-point-system;http://hl7.org/fhir/contact-point-system;4.0.1;ContactPointSystem;ContactPointSystem;active;False;Telecommunications form for contact point.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;phone;Phone;The value is a telephone number used for voice calls. Use of full international numbers starting with + is recommended to enable automatic dialing support but not required.;;;
contact-point-system;http://hl7.org/fhir/contact-point-system;4.0.1;ContactPointSystem;ContactPointSystem;active;False;Telecommunications form for contact point.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;fax;Fax;The value is a fax machine. Use of full international numbers starting with + is recommended to enable automatic dialing support but not required.;;;
contact-point-system;http://hl7.org/fhir/contact-point-system;4.0.1;ContactPointSystem;ContactPointSystem;active;False;Telecommunications form for contact point.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;email;Email;The value is an email address.;;;
contact-point-system;http://hl7.org/fhir/contact-point-system;4.0.1;ContactPointSystem;ContactPointSystem;active;False;Telecommunications form for contact point.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;pager;Pager;The value is a pager number. These may be local pager numbers that are only usable on a particular pager system.;;;
contact-point-system;http://hl7.org/fhir/contact-point-system;4.0.1;ContactPointSystem;ContactPointSystem;active;False;Telecommunications form for contact point.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;url;URL;A contact that is not a phone, fax, pager or email address and is expressed as a URL.  This is intended for various institutional or personal contacts including web sites, blogs, Skype, Twitter, Facebook, etc. Do not use for email addresses.;;;
contact-point-system;http://hl7.org/fhir/contact-point-system;4.0.1;ContactPointSystem;ContactPointSystem;active;False;Telecommunications form for contact point.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;sms;SMS;A contact that can be used for sending an sms message (e.g. mobile phones, some landlines).;;;
contact-point-system;http://hl7.org/fhir/contact-point-system;4.0.1;ContactPointSystem;ContactPointSystem;active;False;Telecommunications form for contact point.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;other;Other;"A contact that is not a phone, fax, page or email address and is not expressible as a URL.  E.g. Internal mail address.  This SHOULD NOT be used for contacts that are expressible as a URL (e.g. Skype, Twitter, Facebook, etc.)  Extensions may be used to distinguish ""other"" contact types.";;;
contact-point-use;http://hl7.org/fhir/contact-point-use;4.0.1;ContactPointUse;ContactPointUse;active;False;Use of contact point.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;home;Home;"A communication contact point at a home; attempted contacts for business purposes might intrude privacy and chances are one will contact family or other household members instead of the person one wishes to call. Typically used with urgent cases, or if no other contacts are available.";;;
contact-point-use;http://hl7.org/fhir/contact-point-use;4.0.1;ContactPointUse;ContactPointUse;active;False;Use of contact point.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;work;Work;An office contact point. First choice for business related contacts during business hours.;;;
contact-point-use;http://hl7.org/fhir/contact-point-use;4.0.1;ContactPointUse;ContactPointUse;active;False;Use of contact point.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;temp;Temp;A temporary contact point. The period can provide more detailed information.;;;
