dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111769;Haigis a0;"The ""Haigis a0"" constant used in IOL calculation";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111770;Haigis a1;"The ""Haigis a1"" constant used in IOL calculation";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111771;Haigis a2;"The ""Haigis a2"" constant used in IOL calculation";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111772;Hoffer pACD Constant;"The ""Hoffer pACD Constant"" used in IOL calculation";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111773;Surgeon Factor;"The ""Surgeon Factor"" constant used in IOL calculation";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111776;Front Of Cornea To Front Of Lens;Anterior chamber depth defined as the front of the cornea to the front of the lens;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111777;Back Of Cornea To Front Of Lens;Anterior chamber depth defined as the back of the cornea to the front of the lens;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111778;Single or Anterior Lens;Refers to the anterior lens when there are two lenses in the eye. The distance, in mm, from the anterior surface of the lens to the posterior surface of the lens;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111779;Posterior Lens;Refers to the posterior lens when there are two lenses in the eye. The distance, in mm, from the anterior surface of the lens to the posterior surface of the lens;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111780;Measurement From This Device;Value obtained from measurements taken by the device creating this SOP Instance;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111781;External Data Source;Value obtained by data transfer from an external source - not from measurements taken by the device providing the value;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111782;Axial Measurements SOP Instance;Axial Measurements DICOM SOP Instance;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111783;Refractive Measurements SOP Instance;Refractive Measurements DICOM SOP Instance;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111786;Standard Deviation of measurements used;Standard Deviation is a simple measure of the variability of a data set;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111787;Signal to Noise Ratio;Signal to Noise Ratio of the data samples taken to create a measurement;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111791;Spherical projection;Projection from 2D image pixels to 3D Cartesian coordinates based on a spherical mathematical model;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111792;Surface contour mapping;"Mapping from 2D image pixels to 3D Cartesian coordinates based on measurements of the retinal surface; e.g. of the retina, derived via a measurement technology such as Optical Coherence Tomography, Ultrasound etc.";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111800;Visual Field 24-2 Test Pattern;"Test pattern, nominally covering an area within 24° of fixation. Consists of 54 test points a minimum of 3° from each meridian and placed 6° apart. The ""-2"" distinguishes this from another 24° pattern (no longer supported)";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111801;Visual Field 10-2 Test Pattern;"Test pattern, nominally covering an area within 10° of fixation. Consists of 68 test points a minimum of 1° from each meridian and placed 2° apart. The ""-2"" in this case indicates its point layout to be similar to the 30-2 and 24-2";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111802;Visual Field 30-2 Test Pattern;"Test pattern consisting of test point locations within 30° of fixation. Consists of 76 test points a minimum of 3° from each meridian and placed 6° apart. The ""-2"" distinguishes this from another 30° pattern (no longer supported)";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111803;Visual Field 60-4 Test Pattern;"Test pattern consisting of 60 test point locations between 30° and 60° of fixation a minimum of 6° from each meridian and placed 12° apart. The ""-4"" distinguishes this from a similar 60° pattern having 4 additional points";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111804;Visual Field Macula Test Pattern;Test pattern consisting of 16 test point locations within 10° of fixation a minimum of 1° from each meridian and placed 2° apart;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111805;Visual Field Central 40 Point Test Pattern;Test pattern consisting of 40 test point locations within 30° of fixation that spread out radially from fixation;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111806;Visual Field Central 76 Point Test Pattern;Test pattern consisting of 76 test point locations within 30° of fixation a minimum of 3° from each meridian and placed 6° apart;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111807;Visual Field Peripheral 60 Point Test Pattern;Test pattern consisting of 60 test point locations between 30° and 60° of fixation a minimum of 6° from each meridian and placed 12° apart;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111808;Visual Field Full Field 81 Point Test Pattern;Test pattern consisting of 81 test point locations within 60° of fixation that spread out radially from fixation;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111809;Visual Field Full Field 120 Point Test Pattern;Test pattern consisting of 120 test point locations within 60° of fixation that spread out radially from fixation, concentrated in the nasal hemisphere;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111810;Visual Field G Test Pattern;Test pattern for Glaucoma and general visual field assessment with 59 test locations of which 16 test locations are in the macular area (up to 10° eccentricity) and where the density of test location is reduced with eccentricity. The test can be extended with the inclusion of 14 test locations between 30° and 60° eccentricity, 6 of which are located at the nasal step;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111811;Visual Field M Test Pattern;Test pattern for the macular area. Orthogonal test pattern with 0.7° spacing within the central 4° of eccentricity and reduced density of test locations between 4 and 10, 5° of eccentricity. 81 test locations over all. The test can be extended to include the test locations of the Visual Field G Test Pattern between 10, 5° and 60°;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111812;Visual Field 07 Test Pattern;Full field test pattern with 48 test locations from 0-30° and 82 test locations from 30-70°. Reduced test point density with increased eccentricity. Can be combined with screening and threshold strategies;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111813;Visual Field LVC Test Pattern;Low Vision Central. Orthogonal off-center test pattern with 6° spacing. 75 test locations within the central 30°. Corresponds with the 32/30-2 excluding the 2 locations at the blind spot, including a macular test location. The LVC is linked with a staircase threshold strategy starting at 0 dB intensity and applies stimulus area V;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111814;Visual Field Central Test Pattern;General test corresponding to the 30-2 but excluding the 2 test locations in the blind spot area, hence with 74 instead of 76 test locations;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111815;Visual Field SITA-Standard Test Strategy;Swedish Interactive Thresholding Algorithm (SITA). Strategy gains testing efficiency through use of visual field and information theory models. In: Bengtsson B, Olsson J, Heijl A, Rootzen H. A new generation of algorithms for computerized threshold perimetry, SITA. Acta Ophthalmologica Scandinavica, 1997, 75: 368-375;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111816;Visual Field SITA-SWAP Test Strategy;Adaptation of SITA testing methods to Blue-Yellow testing;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111817;Visual Field SITA-Fast Test Strategy;Similar to SITA-Standard but with less strict criteria for closing test points. Intended for patients who must be tested in the shortest possible time. In: Bengtsson B, Hejl A. SITA Fast, a new rapid perimetric threshold test. Description of methods and evaluation in patients with manifest and suspect glaucoma. Acta Ophthalmologica Scandinavica, 1998, 76: 431-437;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111818;Visual Field Full Threshold Test Strategy;"Threshold test algorithm that determines a patient's sensitivity at each test point in the threshold test pattern by adjusting intensity by 4 dB steps until the patient changes their response, and then adjusts the intensity in the opposite direction by 2 dB steps until the patient changes their response again. The last stimulus seen by the patient is recognized as the threshold for that point. The starting values are determined by first thresholding a ""primary"" point in each quadrant then using the results of each primary point to determine the starting values for neighboring points";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111819;Visual Field FastPac Test Strategy;Similar to the Full Threshold algorithm except that it steps by 3 dB and only crosses the threshold only once. In: Flanagan JG, Wild JM, Trope GE. Evaluation of FASTPAC, a new strategy for threshold estimation with the Humphrey Field Analyzer, in a glaucomatous population. Ophthalmology, 1993, 100: 949-954;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111820;Visual Field Full From Prior Test Strategy;Identical to Full Threshold except that starting values are determined by the results of a previous test performed using the same test pattern and the Full Threshold test strategy;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111821;Visual Field Optima Test Strategy;Similar to FastPac except that the steps are pseudo-dynamic (differ based on the intensity of the last presentation);;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111822;Visual Field Two-Zone Test Strategy;"Suprathreshold testing strategy, in which each point is initially tested using stimulus that is 6 dB brighter than the expected hill of vision. If the patient does not respond, the stimulus is presented a second time at the same brightness. If the patient sees either presentation, the point is marked as ""seen""; otherwise it is marked as ""not seen""";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111823;Visual Field Three-Zone Test Strategy;An extension of the two-zone strategy in which test points where the second stimulus is not seen are presented with a third stimulus at maximum brightness;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111824;Visual Field Quantify-Defects Test Strategy;An extension of the two-zone strategy, in which test points where the second stimulus is not seen receive threshold testing to quantify the depth of any detected scotomas;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111825;Visual Field TOP Test Strategy;Tendency Oriented Perimetry. Fast thresholding algorithm. Test strategy makes use of the interaction between neighboring test locations to reduce the test time compared to normal full threshold strategy by 60-80%. In: Morales J, Weitzman ML, Gonzalez de la Rosa M. Comparison between Tendency-Oriented Perimetry (TOP) and octopus threshold perimetry. Ophthalmology, 2000, 107: 134-142;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111826;Visual Field Dynamic Test Strategy;Dynamic strategy is a fast thresholding strategy reducing test duration by adapting the dB step sizes according to the frequency-of-seeing curve of the threshold. Reduction of test time compared to normal full threshold strategy 30-50%;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111827;Visual Field Normal Test Strategy;Traditional full threshold staircase strategy. Initial intensities are presented, based on anchor point sensitivities in each quadrant and based on already known neighboring sensitivities. In a first run, thresholds are changed in 4dB steps until the first response reversal. Then the threshold is changed in 2 dB steps until the second response reversal. The threshold is calculated as the average between the last seen and last not-seen stimulus, supposed to correspond with the 50% point in the frequency-of-seeing curve;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111828;Visual Field 1-LT Test Strategy;One level screening test: Each test location is tested with a single intensity. The result is shown as seen or not-seen. The intensity can either be a 0 dB stimulus or a predefined intensity;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111829;Visual Field 2-LT Test Strategy;Two level screening test: Each test location is initially tested 6 dB brighter than the age corrected normal value;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111830;Visual Field LVS Test Strategy;Low Vision Strategy is a full threshold normal strategy with the exception that it starts at 0 dB intensity and applies stimulus area V;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111831;Visual Field GATE Test Strategy;German Adaptive Threshold Estimation is a fast strategy based on a modified 4-2 staircase algorithm, using prior visual fields to calculate the starting intensity. In: Chiefer U, Pascual JP, Edmunds B, Feudner E, Hoffmann EM, Johnson CA, Lagreze WA, Pfeiffer N, Sample PA, Staubach F, Weleber RG, Vonthein R, Krapp E, Paetzold J. Comparison of the new perimetric GATE strategy with conventional full-threshold and SITA standard strategies. Investigative Ophthalmology and Visual Science, 2009, 51: 488-494;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111832;Visual Field GATEi Test Strategy;Similar to GATE. The i stands for initial. If there was no prior visual field test to calculate the starting values, an anchor point method is used to define the local start values;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111833;Visual Field 2LT-Dynamic Test Strategy;A test started as two level screening test. In the course of the test, the threshold of relative defects and/or normal test locations has been quantified using the dynamic threshold strategy;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111834;Visual Field 2LT-Normal Test Strategy;A test started as two level screening test. In the course of the test, the threshold of relative defects and/or normal test locations has been quantified using the normal full threshold strategy;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111835;Visual Field Fast Threshold Test Strategy;Takes neighborhood test point results into account and offers stimuli with an adapted value to save time;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111836;Visual Field CLIP Test Strategy;Continuous Luminance Incremental Perimetry, which measures at first the individual reaction time of the patient and threshold values in every quadrant. The starting value for the main test is slightly below in individual threshold;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111837;Visual Field CLASS Strategy;A supra threshold screening strategy. The starting stimuli intensities depend on the classification of the patient's visual hill by measuring the central (fovea) or peripheral (15° meridian) threshold. The result of each dot slightly underestimates the sensitivity value (within 5 dB);;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111838;Age corrected;Mode for determining the starting luminance for screening test points - the starting luminance s is chosen based on the age of the patient;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111839;Threshold related;"Mode for determining the starting luminance for screening test points - the starting luminance is chosen based on the results of thresholding a set of ""primary"" test points (one in each quadrant)";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111840;Single luminance;Mode for determining the starting luminance for screening test points - in this case, all starting luminance is set to the same value;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111841;Foveal sensitivity related;Mode for determining the starting luminance for screening test points - the starting luminance is chosen based on the result of the foveal threshold value;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111842;Related to non macular sensitivity;Mode for determining the starting luminance for screening test points - the starting luminance is chosen based on the result of four threshold values measured near the 15° meridian (one in each quadrant);;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111843;Automated Optical;Real time evaluation of the camera image to recognize blinks and fixation losses with influence on the test procedure. Blinks that interfere with stimuli presentation cause the automated repetition of such stimulus presentations. Fixation losses can be used to delay the stimulus presentation until correct fixation is regained;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111844;Blind Spot Monitoring;A method of monitoring the patient's fixation by periodically presenting stimulus in a location on the background surface that corresponds to the patient's blind spot;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111845;Macular Fixation Testing;A method of monitoring the patient's fixation by presenting the stimulus to the patient's macula;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111846;Observation by Examiner;A method of monitoring the patient's fixation by observation from the examiner of the patient;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111847;Outside normal limits;Analysis Results are outside normal limits;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111848;Borderline;Analysis Results are borderline;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111849;Abnormally high sensitivity;Analysis Results identify abnormally high sensitivity;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111850;General reduction in sensitivity;Analysis Results identify general reduction in sensitivity;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111851;Borderline and general reduction in sensitivity;Analysis Results identify Borderline and general reduction in sensitivity;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111852;Visual Field Index;Index of a patient's remaining visual field normalized for both age and generalized defect;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111853;Visual Field Loss Due to Diffuse Defect;Estimate of the portion of a patient's visual field loss that is diffuse (i.e., spread evenly across all portions of the visual field);;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111854;Visual Field Loss Due to Local Defect;Estimate of the portion of a patient's visual field loss that is local (i.e., not spread evenly across all portions of the visual field);;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111855;Glaucoma Hemifield Test Analysis;An analysis of asymmetry between zones of the superior and inferior visual field. It is designed to be specific for defects due to glaucoma;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111856;Optical Fixation Measurements;The data output of an optical fixation monitoring process, consisting of a list of positive and negative numbers indicating the quality of patient fixation over the course of a visual field test. The value 0 represents the initial fixation. Negative numbers indicate a measuring error (i.e., the patient blinked). Positive numbers quantify the degree of eccentricity from initial fixation;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111900;Macula centered;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend that is centered on the macula; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111901;Disc centered;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend that is centered on the optic disc; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111902;Lesion centered;"An image of any angular subtend that is centered on a lesion located in any region of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111903;Disc-macula centered;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend centered midway between the disc and macula and containing at least a portion of the disc and both the disc and the macula; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111904;Mid-peripheral-superior;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend positioned between the central zone and the equator, and spanning both the superior-temporal and superior-nasal quadrants of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111905;Mid-peripheral-superior temporal;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend positioned between the central zone and the equator in the superior-temporal quadrant of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111906;Mid-peripheral-temporal;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend positioned between the central zone and the equator, and spanning both the superior-temporal and inferior-temporal quadrants of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111907;Mid-peripheral-inferior temporal;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend positioned between the central zone and the equator in the inferior-temporal quadrant of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111908;Mid-peripheral-inferior;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend positioned between the central zone and the equator, and spanning both the inferior-temporal and inferior-nasal quadrants of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111909;Mid-peripheral-inferior nasal;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend positioned between the central zone and the equator in the inferior-nasal quadrant of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111910;Mid-peripheral-nasal;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend positioned between the central zone and the equator, and spanning both the superior-nasal and inferior-nasal quadrants of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111911;Mid-peripheral-superior nasal;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend positioned between the central zone and the equator in the superior-nasal quadrant of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111912;Peripheral-superior;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend positioned between the equator and the ora serrata, and spanning both the superior temporal and superior nasal quadrants of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111913;Peripheral-superior temporal;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend positioned between the equator and ora serrata in the superior-temporal quadrant of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111914;Peripheral-temporal;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend positioned between the equator and ora serrata, and spanning both the superior-temporal and inferior-temporal quadrants of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111915;Peripheral-inferior temporal;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend positioned between the equator and ora serrata in the inferior-temporal quadrant of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111916;Peripheral-inferior;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend positioned between the equator and ora serrata, and spanning both the inferior-temporal and inferior-nasal quadrants of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111917;Peripheral-inferior nasal;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend positioned between the equator and ora serrata in the inferior-nasal quadrant of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111918;Peripheral-nasal;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend positioned between the equator and ora serrata, and spanning both the superior-nasal and inferior-nasal quadrants of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111919;Peripheral-superior nasal;"An image of at least 15° angular subtend positioned between the equator and ora serrata in the superior-nasal quadrant of the fundus; see Section U.1.8 ""Relative Image Position Definitions"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111920;Time domain;Identifies the use of physical signals with respect to time to capture information;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111921;Spectral domain;Identifies the use of physical signals with respect to multiple frequencies to capture information;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111922;No corneal compensation;No compensation algorithm for corneal birefringence;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111923;Corneal birefringence compensation;Algorithm to compensate for variability in corneal birefringence;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111924;Retinal topography;Measurement of the retinal surface contour relative to an assigned datum plane;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111925;Retinal nerve fiber layer thickness;"Measurement approximating the distance related to the structure between the internal limiting membrane (ILM) and the outer boarder of the retinal nerve fiber layer (RNFL); see Section III.6 ""Retinal Thickness Definition"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111926;Ganglion cell complex thickness;"Measurement approximating the distance related to the structure between the ILM and the outer border of the inner plexiform layer (IPL), called the ganglion cell complex (GCC); see Section III.6 ""Retinal Thickness Definition"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111927;Total retinal thickness (ILM to IS-OS);"Measurement approximating the distance related to the structure between the ILM and the inner-outer segment junction (IS-OS); see Section III.6 ""Retinal Thickness Definition"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111928;Total retinal thickness (ILM to RPE);"Measurement approximating the distance related to the structure between the ILM and the retinal pigment epithelium (RPE); see Section III.6 ""Retinal Thickness Definition"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111929;Total retinal thickness (ILM to BM);"Measurement approximating the distance related to the structure between the ILM and the Bruch's membrane (BM); see Section III.6 ""Retinal Thickness Definition"" in PS3.17";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111930;Absolute ophthalmic thickness;"Thickness of a component of the posterior segment of the eye; e.g. thickness of retina, choroid, etc.";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111931;Thickness deviation category from normative data;Ophthalmic Thickness map based upon statistical significance category (such as percentile) from a normative data set;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111932;Thickness deviation from normative data;Ophthalmic Thickness map based upon deviation (such as microns) from a normative data set;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111933;Related ophthalmic thickness map;Ophthalmic Thickness Map related to another Ophthalmic Thickness Map or another SOP Instance;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111934;Disc-Fovea;An anatomic point centered midway between the disc and fovea centralis;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111935;p>5%;Assuming the null hypothesis is true, the conditional percent probability of observing this result is not statistically significant;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111936;p<5%;Assuming the null hypothesis is true, the conditional percent probability of observing this result is statistically significant, 95% unlikely to happen by chance;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111937;p<2%;Assuming the null hypothesis is true, the conditional percent probability of observing this result is statistically significant, 98% unlikely to happen by chance;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111938;p<1%;Assuming the null hypothesis is true, the conditional percent probability of observing this result is statistically significant, 99% unlikely to happen by chance;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111939;p<0.5%;Assuming the null hypothesis is true, the conditional percent probability of observing this result is statistically significant, 99.5% unlikely to happen by chance;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111940;Corneal axial power map;A two dimensional representation of the axial curvature of the cornea. Axial curvature is calculated from the reciprocal of the distance from a point on a meridian normal at the point to the corneal topographer axis. Also known as sagittal curvature;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111941;Corneal instantaneous power map;A two dimensional representation of the instantaneous curvature of the cornea. Instantaneous curvature is calculated from the reciprocal of the distance from a point on a meridian normal at the point to the center of curvature of that point. Also called tangential curvature;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111942;Corneal refractive power map;A two dimensional representation of the refractive power of the cornea. Corneal refractive power is calculated using Snell's Law;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111943;Corneal elevation map;A two dimensional representation of the elevation of the cornea. Elevation is calculated as the distance from a point on the corneal surface to a point on a reference surface along a line parallel to the corneal topographer axis. For the purpose of visualization the reference surface is usually a sphere or an ellipse;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111944;Corneal wavefront map;A two dimensional representation of a wavefront aberration surface of the cornea. Wavefront aberration surface is calculated from the corneal elevation data fit with either the Zernike polynomial series or the Fourier Series. Maps generally display total aberrations and selectable higher order aberrations;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111945;Elevation-based corneal tomographer;A device that measures corneal anterior surface shape using elevation-based methods (stereographic and light slit-based). Rasterstereography images a grid pattern illuminating the fluorescein dyed tear film with 2 cameras to produce 3D. Slit-based devices scan the cornea, usually by rotation about the instrument axis centered on the cornea vertex;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111946;Reflection-based corneal topographer;A reflection-based device that projects a pattern of light onto the cornea and an image of the reflection of that pattern from the tear film is recorded in one video frame. Light patterns include the circular mire pattern (Placido disc) and spot matrix patterns. Sequential scanning of light spots reflected from the corneal surface is also used requiring multiple video frames for recording;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;111947;Interferometry-based corneal tomographer;"An Interference-based device that projects a beam of light onto and through the cornea. Light reflected from within the cornea is combined with a reference beam giving rise to an interference pattern. Appropriately scanned, this imaging is used to construct 3-dimensional images of the cornea from anterior to posterior surfaces; e.g. swept source OCT";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112000;Chest CAD Report;A structured report containing the results of computer-aided detection or diagnosis applied to chest imaging and associated clinical information;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112001;Opacity;The shadow of an absorber that attenuates the X-Ray beam more effectively than do surrounding absorbers. In a radiograph, any circumscribed area that appears more nearly white (of lesser photometric density) than its surround [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112002;Series Instance UID;A unique identifier for a series of DICOM SOP instances;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112003;Associated Chest Component;A named anatomic region within the chest cavity;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112004;Abnormal interstitial pattern;A collection of opacities detected within the continuum of loose connective tissue throughout the lung, that is not expected in a diagnostically normal radiograph;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112005;Radiographic anatomy;A type of anatomy that is expected to be detectable on a radiographic (X-Ray based) image;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112006;Distribution Descriptor;Characteristic of the extent of spreading of a finding or feature;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112007;Border definition;Characteristic of the clarity of the boundary or edges of a finding or feature;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112008;Site involvement;The part(s) of the anatomy affected or encompassed by a finding or feature;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112009;Type of Content;Characteristic of the matter or substance within a finding or feature;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112010;Texture Descriptor;Characteristic of the surface or consistency of a finding or feature;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112011;Positioner Primary Angle;Position of the X-Ray beam about the patient from the RAO to LAO direction where movement from RAO to vertical is positive;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112012;Positioner Secondary Angle;Position of the X-Ray beam about the patient from the caudal to cranial direction where movement from caudal to vertical is positive;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112013;Location in Chest;The zone, lobe or segment within the chest cavity in which a finding or feature is situated;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112014;Orientation Descriptor;Vertical refers to orientation parallel to the superior-inferior (cephalad-caudad) axis of the body, with horizontal being perpendicular to this, and an oblique orientation having projections in both the horizontal and vertical;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112015;Border shape;Characteristic of the shape formed by the boundary or edges of a finding or feature;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112016;Baseline Category;Indicates whether a finding was considered a target lesion, non-target lesion, or non-lesion during evaluation of a baseline series, according to a method such as RECIST;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112017;Cavity extent as percent of volume;The extent of a detected cavity, represented as the percent of the surrounding volume that it occupies;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112018;Calcification extent as percent of surface;The extent of a detected calcification, represented as the percent of the surrounding surface that it occupies;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112019;Calcification extent as percent of volume;The extent of a detected calcification, represented as the percent of the surrounding volume that it occupies;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112020;Response Evaluation;A heading for the reporting of response evaluation for treatment of solid tumors;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112021;Response Evaluation Method;The system applied in the reporting of response evaluation for treatment of solid tumors;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112022;RECIST;"Response Evaluation Criteria In Solid Tumors; see Normative References";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112023;Composite Feature Modifier;A term that further specifies the name of an item that is an inferred correlation relating two or more individual findings or features;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112024;Single Image Finding Modifier;A term that further specifies the name of an item that was detected on one image;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112025;Size Descriptor;A qualitative descriptor for the extent of a finding or feature;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112026;Width Descriptor;A qualitative descriptor for the thickness of tubular structures, such as blood vessels;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112027;Opacity Descriptor;A characteristic that further describes the nature of an opacity;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112028;Abnormal Distribution of Anatomic Structure;The type of adverse affect that a finding or feature is having on the surrounding anatomy;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112029;WHO;"Response evaluation method as defined in chapter 5, ""Reporting of Response"" of the WHO Handbook for Reporting Results for Cancer Treatment; see Normative References";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112030;Calcification Descriptor;Identification of the morphology of detected calcifications;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112031;Attenuation Coefficient;A quantitative numerical statement of the relative attenuation of the X-Ray beam at a specified point. Coefficient that describes the fraction of a beam of X-Rays or gamma rays that is absorbed or scattered per unit thickness of the absorber. This value basically accounts for the number of atoms in a cubic cm volume of material and the probability of a photon being scattered or absorbed from the nucleus or an electron of one of these atoms. Usually expressed in Hounsfield units [referred to as CT Number in Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112032;Threshold Attenuation Coefficient;"An X-Ray attenuation coefficient that is used as a threshold; e.g. in calcium scoring";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112033;Abnormal opacity;An opacity that is not expected in a diagnostically normal radiograph;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112034;Calculation Description;A textual description of the mathematical method of calculation that resulted in a calculated value;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112035;Performance of Pediatric and Adult Chest Radiography, ACR;American College of Radiology. ACR Standard for the Performance of Pediatric and Adult Chest Radiography. In: Standards. Reston, Va: 2001:95-98;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112036;ACR Position Statement;American College of Radiology. ACR Position Statement for Quality Control and Improvement, Safety, Infection Control, and Patient Concerns. In: Practice Guidelines and Technical Standards. Reston, Va: 2001:iv;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112037;Non-lesion Modifier;A descriptor for a non-lesion object finding or feature, used to indicate whether the object was detected as being internal or external to the patient's body;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112038;Osseous Modifier;A concept modifier for an Osseous Anatomy, or bone related, finding;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112039;Tracking Identifier;A text label used for tracking a finding or feature, potentially across multiple reporting objects, over time. This label shall be unique within the domain in which it is used;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112040;Tracking Unique Identifier;A unique identifier used for tracking a finding or feature, potentially across multiple reporting objects, over time;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112041;Target Lesion Complete Response;Disappearance of all target lesions;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112042;Target Lesion Partial Response;At least a 30% decrease in the sum of the Longest Diameter of target lesions, taking as reference the baseline sum Longest Diameter;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112043;Target Lesion Progressive Disease;At least a 20% increase in the sum of the Longest Diameter of target lesions, taking as reference the smallest sum Longest Diameter recorded since the treatment started, or the appearance of one or more new lesions;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112044;Target Lesion Stable Disease;Neither sufficient shrinkage to qualify for Partial Response nor sufficient increase to qualify for Progressive Disease, taking as reference the smallest sum Longest Diameter since the treatment started;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112045;Non-Target Lesion Complete Response;Disappearance of all non-target lesions and normalization of tumor marker level;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112046;Non-Target Lesion Incomplete Response or Stable Disease;Persistence of one or more non-target lesions and/or maintenance of tumor marker level above the normal limits;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112047;Non-Target Lesion Progressive Disease;Appearance of one or more new lesions and/or unequivocal progression of existing non-target lesions;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112048;Current Response;The current response evaluation for treatment of solid tumors, according to a method such as RECIST;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112049;Best Overall Response;Best response recorded from the start of the treatment until disease progression/recurrence, taking as reference for Progressive Disease the smallest measurements recorded since the treatment started, according to a method such as RECIST;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112050;Anatomic Identifier;"A text identifier of an anatomic feature when a multiplicity of features of that type may be present, such as ""Rib 1"", ""Rib 2"" or thoracic vertebrae ""T1"" or ""T2""";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112051;Measurement of Response;"A measured or calculated evaluation of response; e.g. according to a method such as RECIST, the value would be the calculated sum of the lengths of the longest axes of a set of target lesions";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112052;Bronchovascular;Of or relating to a bronchial (lung) specific channel for the conveyance of a body fluid;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112053;Osseous;Of, relating to, or composed of bone;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112054;Secondary pulmonary lobule;"The smallest unit of lung surrounded by connective tissue septa; the unit of lung subtended by any bronchiole that gives off three to five terminal bronchioles [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112055;Agatston scoring method;A method of calculating an overall calcium score, reflecting the calcification of coronary arteries, based on the maximum X-Ray attenuation coefficient and the area of calcium deposits;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112056;Volume scoring method;A method of calculating an overall calcium score, reflecting the calcification of coronary arteries, based on the volume of each calcification, typically expressed in mm3;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112057;Mass scoring method;A method of calculating an overall calcium score, reflecting the calcification of coronary arteries, based on the total mass of calcification, typically expressed in mg;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112058;Calcium score;A measure often arrived at through calculation of findings from CT examination, which is a common predictor of significant stenosis of the coronary arteries;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112059;Primary complex;The combination of a focus of pneumonia due to a primary infection with granulomas in the draining hilar or mediastinal lymph nodes [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112060;Oligemia;General or local decrease in the apparent width of visible pulmonary vessels, suggesting less than normal blood flow (reduced blood flow) [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112061;Abnormal lines (1D);Linear opacity of very fine width, i.e., a nearly one dimensional opacity;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112062;Abnormal lucency;Area of abnormal very low X-Ray attenuation, typically lower than aerated lung when occurring in or projecting over lung, or lower than soft tissue when occurring in or projecting over soft tissue;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112063;Abnormal calcifications;A calcific opacity within the lung that may be organized, but does not display the trabecular organization of true bone [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112064;Abnormal texture;Relatively homogeneous, extended, pattern of abnormal opacity in the lung, typically low in contrast;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112065;Reticulonodular pattern;A collection of innumerable small, linear, and nodular opacities that together produce a composite appearance resembling a net with small superimposed nodules. The reticular and nodular elements are dimensionally of similar magnitude [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112066;Beaded septum sign;"Irregular septal thickening that suggests the appearance of a row of beads; usually a sign of lymphangitic carcinomatosis, but may also occur rarely in sarcoidosis [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112067;Nodular pattern;A collection of innumerable, small discrete opacities ranging in diameter from 2-10 mm, generally uniform in size and widespread in distribution, and without marginal spiculation [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112068;Pseudoplaque;An irregular band of peripheral pulmonary opacity adjacent to visceral pleura that simulates the appearance of a pleural plaque and is formed by coalescence of small nodules [Fraser and Pare] ;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112069;Signet-ring sign;"A ring of opacities (usually representing a dilated, thick-walled bronchus) in association with a smaller, round, soft tissue opacity (the adjacent pulmonary artery) suggesting a ""signet ring"" [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112070;Air bronchiologram;Equivalent of air bronchogram, but in airways assumed to be bronchioles because of peripheral location and diameter [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112071;Air bronchogram;"Radiographic shadow of an air-containing bronchus; presumed to represent an air-containing segment of the bronchial tree (identity often inferred) [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112072;Air crescent;Air in a crescentic shape in a nodule or mass, in which the air separates the outer wall of the lesion from an inner sequestrum, which most commonly is a fungus ball of Aspergillusspecies [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112073;Halo sign;Ground-glass opacity surrounding the circumference of a nodule or mass. May be a sign of invasive aspergillosis or hemorrhage of various causes [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112074;Target Lesion at Baseline;Flag denoting that this lesion was identified, at baseline, as a target lesion intended for tracking over time [RECIST];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112075;Non-Target Lesion at Baseline;Flag denoting that this lesion was not identified, at baseline, as a target lesion, and was not intended for tracking over time [RECIST];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112076;Non-Lesion at Baseline;Flag denoting that this finding was identified, at baseline, as a category other than a lesion, and was not intended for tracking over time [RECIST];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112077;Vasoconstriction;Local or general reduction in the caliber of visible pulmonary vessels, presumed to result from decreased flow occasioned by contraction of muscular pulmonary arteries [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112078;Vasodilation;Local or general increase in the width of visible pulmonary vessels resulting from increased pulmonary blood flow [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112079;Architectural distortion;A manifestation of lung disease in which bronchi, pulmonary vessels, a fissure or fissures, or septa of secondary pulmonary lobules are abnormally displaced [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112080;Mosaic perfusion;A patchwork of regions of varied attenuation, interpreted as secondary to regional differences in perfusion [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112081;Pleonemia;Increased blood flow to the lungs or a portion thereof, manifested by a general or local increase in the width of visible pulmonary vessels [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112082;Interface;The common boundary between the shadows of two juxtaposed structures or tissues of different texture or opacity (edge, border) [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112083;Line;A longitudinal opacity no greater than 2 mm in width [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112084;Lucency;The shadow of an absorber that attenuates the primary X-Ray beam less effectively than do surrounding absorbers. In a radiograph, any circumscribed area that appears more nearly black (of greater photometric density) than its surround [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112085;Midlung window;A midlung region, characterized by the absence of large blood vessels and by a paucity of small blood vessels, that corresponds to the minor fissure and adjacent peripheral lung [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112086;Carina angle;The angle formed by the right and left main bronchi at the tracheal bifurcation [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112087;Centrilobular structures;"The pulmonary artery and its immediate branches in a secondary lobule; HRCT depicts these vessels in certain cases; a.k.a. core structures or lobular core structures [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112088;Anterior junction line;A vertically oriented linear or curvilinear opacity approximately 1-2 mm wide, commonly projected on the tracheal air shadow [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112089;Posterior junction line;A vertically oriented, linear or curvilinear opacity approximately 2 mm wide, commonly projected on the tracheal air shadow, and usually slightly concave to the right [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112090;Azygoesophageal recess interface;A space in the right side of the mediastinum into which the medial edge of the right lower lobe extends [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112091;Paraspinal line;A vertically oriented interface usually seen in a frontal chest radiograph to the left of the thoracic vertebral column [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112092;Posterior tracheal stripe;A vertically oriented linear opacity ranging in width from 2-5 mm, extending from the thoracic inlet to the bifurcation of the trachea, and visible only on lateral radiographs of the chest [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112093;Right tracheal stripe;A vertically oriented linear opacity approximately 2-3 mm wide extending from the thoracic inlet to the right tracheobronchial angle [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112094;Stripe;"A longitudinal composite opacity measuring 2-5 mm in width; acceptable when limited to anatomic structures within the mediastinum [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112095;Hiatus;"A gap or passage through an anatomical part or organ; especially : a gap through which another part or organ passes";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112096;Rib Scalene Tubercle;A small rounded elevation or eminence on the first rib for the attachment of the scalenus anterior;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112097;Vertebral Intervertebral Notch;A groove that serves for the transmission of the vertebral artery;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112098;Subscapular Fossa;The concave depression of the anterior surface of the scapula;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112099;Scapular Spine;A sloping ridge dividing the dorsal surface of the scapula into the supraspinatous fossa (above), and the infraspinatous fossa (below);;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112100;Scapular Supraspinatus Fossa;The portion of the dorsal surface of the scapula above the scapular spine;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112101;Scapular Infraspinatus Fossa;The portion of the dorsal surface of the scapula below the scapular spine;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112102;Aortic knob;The portion of the aortic arch that defines the transition between its ascending and descending limbs;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112103;Arch of the Azygos vein;Section of Azygos vein near the fourth thoracic vertebra, where it arches forward over the root of the right lung, and ends in the superior vena cava, just before that vessel pierces the pericardium;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112104;Air-fluid level;A local collection of gas and liquid that, when traversed by a horizontal X-Ray beam, creates a shadow characterized by a sharp horizontal interface between gas density above and liquid density below [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112105;Corona radiata;A circumferential pattern of fine linear spicules, approximately 5 mm long, extending outward from the margin of a solitary pulmonary nodule through a zone of relative lucency [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112106;Honeycomb pattern;"A number of closely approximated ring shadows representing air spaces 5-10 mm in diameter with walls 2-3 mm thick that resemble a true honeycomb; implies ""end-stage"" lung [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112107;Fleischner's line(s);"A straight, curved, or irregular linear opacity that is visible in multiple projections; usually situated in the lower half of the lung; vary markedly in length and width [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112108;Intralobular lines;Fine linear opacities present in a lobule when the intralobular interstitium is thickened. When numerous, they may appear as a fine reticular pattern [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112109;Kerley A line;Essentially straight linear opacity 2-6 cm in length and 1-3 mm in width, usually in an upper lung zone [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112110;Kerley B line;A straight linear opacity 1.5-2 cm in length and 1-2 mm in width, usually at the lung base [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112111;Kerley C lines;A group of branching, linear opacities producing the appearing of a fine net, at the lung base [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112112;Parenchymal band;Elongated opacity, usually several millimeters wide and up to about 5 cm long, often extending to the pleura, which may be thickened and retracted at the site of contact [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112113;Reticular pattern;A collection of innumerable small linear opacities that together produce an appearance resembling a net [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112114;Septal line(s);Usually used in the plural, a generic term for linear opacities of varied distribution produced when the interstitium between pulmonary lobules is thickened [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112115;Subpleural line;A thin curvilinear opacity, a few millimeters or less in thickness, usually less than 1 cm from the pleural surface and paralleling the pleura [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112116;Tramline shadow;Parallel or slightly convergent linear opacities that suggest the planar projection of tubular structures and that correspond in location and orientation to elements of the bronchial tree [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112117;Tubular shadow;"Paired, parallel, or slightly convergent linear opacities presumed to represent the walls of a tubular structure seen en face; used if the anatomic nature of a shadow is obscure [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112118;Density;"The opacity of a radiographic shadow to visible light; film blackening; the term should never be used to mean an ""opacity"" or ""radiopacity"" [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112119;Dependent opacity;"Subpleural increased attenuation in dependent lung. The increased attenuation disappears when the region of lung is nondependent; a.k.a. dependent increased attenuation [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112120;Ground glass opacity;"Hazy increased attenuation of lung, but with preservation of bronchial and vascular margins; caused by partial filling of air spaces, interstitial thickening, partial collapse of alveoli, normal expiration, or increased capillary blood volume [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112121;Infiltrate;Any ill-defined opacity in the lung [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112122;Micronodule;Discrete, small, round, focal opacity of at least soft tissue attenuation and with a diameter no greater than 7 mm [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112123;Phantom tumor (pseudotumor);A shadow produced by a local collection of fluid in one of the interlobar fissures, usually elliptic in one radiographic projection and rounded in the other, resembling a tumor [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112124;Shadow;"Any perceptible discontinuity in film blackening attributed to the attenuation of the X-Ray beam by a specific anatomic absorber or lesion on or within the body of the patient; to be employed only when more specific identification is not possible [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112125;Small irregular opacities;Term used to define a reticular pattern specific to pneumoconioses [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112126;Small rounded opacities;Term used to define a nodular pattern specific to pneumoconioses [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112127;Tree-in-bud sign;Nodular dilation of centrilobular branching structures that resembles a budding tree and represents exudative bronchiolar dilation [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112128;Granular pattern;Any extended, finely granular pattern of pulmonary opacity within which normal anatomic details are partly obscured [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112129;Miliary pattern;A collection of tiny discrete opacities in the lungs, each measuring 2 mm or less in diameter, generally uniform in size and widespread in distribution [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112130;Mosaic pattern;Generalized pattern of relatively well defined areas in the lung having different X-Ray attenuations due to a longstanding underlying pulmonary disease;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112131;Extremely small;A qualitative descriptor of a size that is dramatically less than typical;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112132;Very small;A qualitative descriptor of a size that is considerably less than typical;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112133;Too small;A qualitative descriptor of a size that is so small as to be abnormal versus expected size;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112134;Elliptic;Shaped like an ellipse (oval);;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112135;Lobulated;A border shape that is made up of, provided with, or divided into lobules (small lobes, curved or rounded projections or divisions);;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112136;Spiculated;Radially orientated border shape;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112137;Sharply defined;The border of a shadow (opacity) is sharply defined [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112138;Distinctly defined;The border of a shadow (opacity) is distinctly defined [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112139;Well demarcated;The border of a shadow (opacity) is well distinct from adjacent structures [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112140;Sharply demarcated;The border of a shadow (opacity) is sharply distinct from adjacent structures [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112141;Poorly demarcated;The border of a shadow (opacity) is poorly distinct from adjacent structures [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112142;Circumscribed;A shadow (opacity) possessing a complete or nearly complete visible border [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112143;Air;Inspired atmospheric gas. The word is sometimes used to describe gas within the body regardless of its composition or site [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112144;Soft tissue;Material having X-Ray attenuation properties similar to muscle;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112145;Calcium;Material having X-Ray attenuation properties similar to calcium, a silver-white bivalent metallic element occurring in plants and animals;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112146;Acinar;A pulmonary opacity 4-8 mm in diameter, presumed to represent anatomic acinus, or a collection of opacities in the lung, each measuring 4-8 mm in diameter, and together producing an extended, homogeneous shadow [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112147;Air space;The gas-containing portion of the lung parenchyma, including the acini and excluding the interstitium [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112148;Fibronodular;Sharply defined, approximately circular opacities occurring singly or in clusters, usually in the upper lobes [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112149;Fluffy;A shadow (opacity) that is ill-defined, lacking clear-cut margins [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112150;Linear;"A shadow resembling a line; any elongated opacity of approximately uniform width [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112151;Profusion;The number of small opacities per unit area or zone of lung. In the International Labor Organization (ILO) classification of radiographs of the pneumoconioses, the qualifiers 0 through 3 subdivide the profusion into 4 categories. The profusion categories may be further subdivided by employing a 12-point scale [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112152;Silhouette sign;"The effacement of an anatomic soft tissue border by either a normal anatomic structure or a pathologic state such as airlessness of adjacent lung or accumulation of fluid in the contiguous pleural space; useful in detecting and localizing an opacity along the axis of the X-Ray beam [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112153;Subpleural;Situated or occurring between the pleura and the body wall;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112154;Bat's wing distribution;"Spatial arrangement of opacities that bears vague resemblance to the shape of a bat in flight; bilaterally symmetric [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112155;Butterfly distribution;"Spatial arrangement of opacities that bears vague resemblance to the shape of a butterfly in flight; bilaterally symmetric [Fraser and Pare]";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112156;Centrilobular;Referring to the region of the bronchioloarteriolar core of a secondary pulmonary lobule [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112157;Coalescent;The joining together of a number of opacities into a single opacity [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112158;Lobar;"Of or relating to a lobe (a curved or rounded projection or division); e.g. involving an entire lobe of the lung";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112159;Hyper-acute;Extremely or excessively acute, as a qualitative measure of severity;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112160;Homogeneous (uniform opacity);Of uniform opacity or texture throughout [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112161;Inhomogeneous;Lack of homogeneity in opacity or texture;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112162;Target;Discrete opacity centrally within a larger opacity, as a calcification descriptor;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112163;Fibrocalcific;Pertaining to sharply defined, linear, and/or nodular opacities containing calcification(s) [Fraser and Pare];;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112164;Flocculent;Calcifications made up of loosely aggregated particles, resembling wool;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112165;Difference in border shape;A change in the shape formed by the boundary or edges of a finding or feature;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112166;Difference in border definition;A change in the clarity of the boundary or edges of a finding or feature;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112167;Difference in distribution;A change in the extent of spreading of a finding or feature;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112168;Difference in site involvement;A change in the part(s) of the anatomy affected or encompassed by a finding or feature;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112169;Difference in Type of Content;A change in the matter or substance within a finding or feature;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112170;Difference in Texture;A change in the surface or consistency of a finding or feature;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112171;Fiducial mark;A location in image space, which may or may not correspond to an anatomical reference, which is often used for registering data sets;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112172;Portacath;"Connected to an injection chamber placed under the skin in the upper part of the chest. When it is necessary to inject some drug, a specific needle is put in the chamber through the skin and a silicon membrane. The advantage of a portacath is that it may be left in place several months contrarily of ""classical"" catheters";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112173;Chest tube;A tube inserted into the chest wall from outside the body, for drainage. Sometimes used for collapsed lung. Usually connected to a receptor placed lower than the insertion site;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112174;Central line;A tube placed into the subclavian vein to deliver medication directly into the venous system;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112175;Kidney stent;A stent is a tube inserted into another tube. Kidney stent is a tube that is inserted into the kidney, ureter, and bladder, to help drain urine. Usually inserted through a scoping device presented through the urethra;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112176;Pancreatic stent;A stent is a tube inserted into another tube. Pancreatic stent is inserted through the common bile duct to the pancreatic duct, to drain bile;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112177;Nipple ring;A non-lesion object that appears to be a circular band, attached to the body via pierced nipple;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112178;Coin;A non-lesion object that appears to be a flat round piece of metal;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112179;Minimum Attenuation Coefficient;"The least quantity assignable, admissible, or possible; the least of a set of X-Ray attenuation coefficients";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112180;Maximum Attenuation Coefficient;"The greatest quantity or value attainable or attained; the largest of a set of X-Ray attenuation coefficients";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112181;Mean Attenuation Coefficient;The value that is computed by dividing the sum of a set of X-Ray attenuation coefficients by the number of values ;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112182;Median Attenuation Coefficient;The value in an ordered set of X-Ray attenuation coefficients, below and above which there is an equal number of values;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112183;Standard Deviation of Attenuation Coefficient;"For a set of X-Ray attenuation coefficients: 1) a measure of the dispersion of a frequency distribution that is the square root of the arithmetic mean of the squares of the deviation of each of the class frequencies from the arithmetic mean of the frequency distribution; 2) a parameter that indicates the way in which a probability function or a probability density function is centered around its mean and that is equal to the square root of the moment in which the deviation from the mean is squared";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;112184;Performance of Pediatric and Adult Thoracic CT;American College of Radiology. ACR Standard for the Performance of Pediatric and Adult Thoracic Computed Tomography (CT). In: Standards. Reston, Va: 2001:103-107;;;
