dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113842;X-Ray Modulation Type;The type of exposure modulation used for the purpose of limiting the dose;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113845;Exposure Index;"Measure of the detector response to radiation in the relevant image region of an image acquired with a digital X-Ray imaging system as defined in IEC 62494-1; see PS3.3 definition of Exposure Index Macro";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113846;Target Exposure Index;"The target value used to calculate the Deviation Index as defined in IEC 62494-1; see PS3.3 definition of Exposure Index Macro";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113847;Deviation Index;"A scaled representation of the accuracy of the Exposure Index compared to the Target Exposure Index as defined in IEC 62494-1; see PS3.3 definition of Exposure Index Macro";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113850;Irradiation Authorizing;The clinician responsible for determining that the irradiating procedure was appropriate for the indications;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113851;Irradiation Administering;The person responsible for the administration of radiation;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113852;Irradiation Event;"An irradiation event is the loading of X-Ray equipment caused by a single continuous actuation of the equipment's irradiation switch, from the start of the loading time of the first pulse until the loading time trailing edge of the final pulse. Any automatic on-off switching of the irradiation source during the event is not treated as separate events, rather the event includes the time between start and stop of irradiation as triggered by the user; e.g. a pulsed fluoro X-Ray acquisition shall be treated as a single irradiation event";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113853;Irradiation Event UID;Unique Identifier of an Irradiation Event;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113854;Source of Dose Information;Method by which dose-related details of an Irradiation Event were obtained;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113855;Total Acquisition Time;Total accumulated acquisition clock time in the scope of the including report (i.e., the sum of the Irradiation Duration values for accumulated acquisition irradiation events);;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113856;Automated Data Collection;Direct recording of data by a relevant system;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113857;Manual Entry;Recording of data by a human operator, including manual transcription of electronic data;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113858;MPPS Content;The data is taken from an MPPS SOP Instance;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113859;Irradiating Device;A device exposing a patient to ionizing radiation;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113860;15cm from Isocenter toward Source;"15cm from the isocenter towards the X-Ray source; See IEC 60601-2-43";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113861;30cm in Front of Image Input Surface;"30cm in front (towards the tube) of the input surface of the image receptor; See FDA Federal Performance Standard for Diagnostic X-Ray Systems §1020.32(d) (7)";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113862;1cm above Tabletop;"1cm above the patient tabletop or cradle; See FDA Federal Performance Standard for Diagnostic X-Ray Systems §1020.32(d) (7)";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113863;30cm above Tabletop;"30cm above the patient tabletop of cradle; See FDA Federal Performance Standard for Diagnostic X-Ray Systems §1020.32(d) (7)";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113864;15cm from Table Centerline;"15cm from the centerline of the X-Ray table and in the direction of the X-Ray source; See FDA Federal Performance Standard for Diagnostic X-Ray Systems §1020.32(d) (7)";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113865;Entrance exposure to a 4.2 cm breast thickness;"Standard breast means a 4.2 centimeter (cm) thick compressed breast consisting of 50 percent glandular and 50 percent adipose tissue. See Department of Health and Human Services, Food and Drug Administration. Mammography quality standards; final rule. Federal Register. Oct. 28, 1997; 68(208):55852-55994; see 900.2(uu)";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113866;Copied From Image Attributes;"The data is copied from information present in the image attributes; e.g. dose attributes such as CTDIvol (0018,9345)";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113867;Computed From Image Attributes;"The data is computed from information present in the image attributes; e.g. by using dosimetry information for the specific irradiating device make and model, applied to technique information such as KVP and mAs";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113868;Derived From Human-Readable Reports;"The data is derived from human-readable reports; e.g. by natural language parsing of text reports, or optical character recognition from reports saved as images by the irradiating device";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113870;Person Name;The name of a specific person;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113871;Person ID;An identification number or code for a specific person;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113872;Person ID Issuer;The organization that issued a Person ID;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113873;Organization Name;The name of an organization;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113874;Person Role in Organization;The role played by a person in an organization;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113875;Person Role in Procedure;The role played by a person in a procedure;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113876;Device Role in Procedure;The role played by a device in a procedure;;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113877;Device Name;"The name used to refer to a device; usually locally unique";;;
dicom-dcim;http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM;01;DICOM Controlled Terminology Definitions;;active;;"DICOM Code Definitions (Coding Scheme Designator ""DCM"" Coding Scheme Version ""01"")";2015-04-20;NEMA/DICOM;complete;113878;Device Manufacturer;Manufacturer of a device;;;
