imagingstudy-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/imagingstudy-status;4.0.1;ImagingStudyStatus;ImagingStudyStatus;draft;False;The status of the ImagingStudy.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;entered-in-error;Entered in Error;"The imaging study has been withdrawn following a previous final release.  This electronic record should never have existed, though it is possible that real-world decisions were based on it. (If real-world activity has occurred, the status should be ""cancelled"" rather than ""entered-in-error"".).";;;
imagingstudy-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/imagingstudy-status;4.0.1;ImagingStudyStatus;ImagingStudyStatus;draft;False;The status of the ImagingStudy.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;unknown;Unknown;"The system does not know which of the status values currently applies for this request. Note: This concept is not to be used for ""other"" - one of the listed statuses is presumed to apply, it's just not known which one.";;;
immunization-evaluation-dose-status-reason;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-evaluation-dose-status-reason;4.0.1;ImmunizationEvaluationDoseStatusReasonCodes;Immunization Evaluation Dose Status Reason codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the reason why an administered dose has been assigned a particular status. Often, this reason describes why a dose is considered invalid. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;advstorage;Adverse storage condition;The product was stored in a manner inconsistent with manufacturer guidelines potentially reducing the effectiveness of the product.;;;
immunization-evaluation-dose-status-reason;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-evaluation-dose-status-reason;4.0.1;ImmunizationEvaluationDoseStatusReasonCodes;Immunization Evaluation Dose Status Reason codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the reason why an administered dose has been assigned a particular status. Often, this reason describes why a dose is considered invalid. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;coldchbrk;Cold chain break;The product was stored at a temperature inconsistent with manufacturer guidelines potentially reducing the effectiveness of the product.;;;
immunization-evaluation-dose-status-reason;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-evaluation-dose-status-reason;4.0.1;ImmunizationEvaluationDoseStatusReasonCodes;Immunization Evaluation Dose Status Reason codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the reason why an administered dose has been assigned a particular status. Often, this reason describes why a dose is considered invalid. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;explot;Expired lot;The product was administered after the expiration date associated with lot of vaccine.;;;
immunization-evaluation-dose-status-reason;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-evaluation-dose-status-reason;4.0.1;ImmunizationEvaluationDoseStatusReasonCodes;Immunization Evaluation Dose Status Reason codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the reason why an administered dose has been assigned a particular status. Often, this reason describes why a dose is considered invalid. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;outsidesched;Administered outside recommended schedule;The product was administered at a time inconsistent with the documented schedule.;;;
immunization-evaluation-dose-status-reason;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-evaluation-dose-status-reason;4.0.1;ImmunizationEvaluationDoseStatusReasonCodes;Immunization Evaluation Dose Status Reason codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the reason why an administered dose has been assigned a particular status. Often, this reason describes why a dose is considered invalid. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;prodrecall;Product recall;The product administered has been recalled by the manufacturer.;;;
immunization-evaluation-dose-status;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-evaluation-dose-status;4.0.1;ImmunizationEvaluationDoseStatusCodes;Immunization Evaluation Dose Status codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the validity of a dose relative to a particular recommended schedule. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;valid;Valid;The dose counts toward fulfilling a path to immunity for a patient, providing protection against the target disease.;;;
immunization-evaluation-dose-status;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-evaluation-dose-status;4.0.1;ImmunizationEvaluationDoseStatusCodes;Immunization Evaluation Dose Status codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the validity of a dose relative to a particular recommended schedule. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;notvalid;Not valid;The dose does not count toward fulfilling a path to immunity for a patient.;;;
immunization-funding-source;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-funding-source;4.0.1;ImmunizationFundingSource;Immunization Funding Source;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the source of the vaccine administered. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;private;Private;The vaccine was purchased with private funds.;;;
immunization-funding-source;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-funding-source;4.0.1;ImmunizationFundingSource;Immunization Funding Source;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the source of the vaccine administered. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;public;Public;The vaccine was purchased with public funds.;;;
immunization-origin;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-origin;4.0.1;ImmunizationOriginCodes;Immunization Origin Codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the source of the data when the report of the immunization event is not based on information from the person, entity or organization who administered the vaccine. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;provider;Other Provider;The data for the immunization event originated with another provider.;;;
immunization-origin;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-origin;4.0.1;ImmunizationOriginCodes;Immunization Origin Codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the source of the data when the report of the immunization event is not based on information from the person, entity or organization who administered the vaccine. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;record;Written Record;The data for the immunization event originated with a written record for the patient.;;;
immunization-origin;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-origin;4.0.1;ImmunizationOriginCodes;Immunization Origin Codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the source of the data when the report of the immunization event is not based on information from the person, entity or organization who administered the vaccine. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;recall;Parent/Guardian/Patient Recall;The data for the immunization event originated from the recollection of the patient or parent/guardian of the patient.;;;
immunization-origin;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-origin;4.0.1;ImmunizationOriginCodes;Immunization Origin Codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the source of the data when the report of the immunization event is not based on information from the person, entity or organization who administered the vaccine. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;school;School Record;The data for the immunization event originated with a school record for the patient.;;;
immunization-origin;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-origin;4.0.1;ImmunizationOriginCodes;Immunization Origin Codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the source of the data when the report of the immunization event is not based on information from the person, entity or organization who administered the vaccine. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;jurisdiction;Jurisdictional IIS;The data for the immunization event originated with an immunization information system (IIS) or registry operating within the jurisdiction.;;;
immunization-program-eligibility;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-program-eligibility;4.0.1;ImmunizationProgramEligibility;Immunization Program Eligibility;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the patient's eligibility for a vaccination program. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;ineligible;Not Eligible;The patient is not eligible for the funding program.;;;
immunization-program-eligibility;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-program-eligibility;4.0.1;ImmunizationProgramEligibility;Immunization Program Eligibility;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the patient's eligibility for a vaccination program. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;uninsured;Uninsured;The patient is eligible for the funding program because they are uninsured.;;;
immunization-recommendation-status;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-recommendation-status;4.0.1;ImmunizationRecommendationStatusCodes;Immunization Recommendation Status Codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the status of the patient towards perceived immunity against a vaccine preventable disease. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;due;Due;The patient is due for their next vaccination.;;;
immunization-recommendation-status;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-recommendation-status;4.0.1;ImmunizationRecommendationStatusCodes;Immunization Recommendation Status Codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the status of the patient towards perceived immunity against a vaccine preventable disease. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;overdue;Overdue;The patient is considered overdue for their next vaccination.;;;
immunization-recommendation-status;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-recommendation-status;4.0.1;ImmunizationRecommendationStatusCodes;Immunization Recommendation Status Codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the status of the patient towards perceived immunity against a vaccine preventable disease. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;immune;Immune;The patient is immune to the target disease and further immunization against the disease is not likely to provide benefit.;;;
immunization-recommendation-status;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-recommendation-status;4.0.1;ImmunizationRecommendationStatusCodes;Immunization Recommendation Status Codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the status of the patient towards perceived immunity against a vaccine preventable disease. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;contraindicated;Contraindicated;The patient is contraindicated for futher doses.;;;
immunization-recommendation-status;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-recommendation-status;4.0.1;ImmunizationRecommendationStatusCodes;Immunization Recommendation Status Codes;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the status of the patient towards perceived immunity against a vaccine preventable disease. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;complete;Complete;The patient is fully protected and no further doses are recommended.;;;
immunization-subpotent-reason;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-subpotent-reason;4.0.1;ImmunizationSubpotentReason;Immunization Subpotent Reason;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the reason why a dose is considered to be subpotent. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;partial;Partial Dose;The full volume of the dose was not administered to the patient.;;;
immunization-subpotent-reason;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-subpotent-reason;4.0.1;ImmunizationSubpotentReason;Immunization Subpotent Reason;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the reason why a dose is considered to be subpotent. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;coldchainbreak;Cold Chain Break;The vaccine experienced a cold chain break.;;;
immunization-subpotent-reason;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/immunization-subpotent-reason;4.0.1;ImmunizationSubpotentReason;Immunization Subpotent Reason;draft;False;The value set to instantiate this attribute should be drawn from a terminologically robust code system that consists of or contains concepts to support describing the reason why a dose is considered to be subpotent. This value set is provided as a suggestive example.;;FHIR Project team;complete;recall;Manufacturer Recall;The vaccine was recalled by the manufacturer.;;;
implantStatus;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/implantStatus;4.0.1;Implant Status;Implant Status;draft;False;A set codes that define the functional status of an implanted device.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;functional;Functional;The implanted device is working normally.;;;
implantStatus;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/implantStatus;4.0.1;Implant Status;Implant Status;draft;False;A set codes that define the functional status of an implanted device.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;non-functional;Non-Functional;The implanted device is not working.;;;
implantStatus;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/implantStatus;4.0.1;Implant Status;Implant Status;draft;False;A set codes that define the functional status of an implanted device.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;disabled;Disabled;The implanted device has been turned off.;;;
implantStatus;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/implantStatus;4.0.1;Implant Status;Implant Status;draft;False;A set codes that define the functional status of an implanted device.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;unknown;Unknown;the functional status of the implant has not been determined.;;;
insuranceplan-applicability;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/applicability;4.0.1;BenefitCostApplicability;Benefit cost applicability;draft;False;Whether the cost applies to in-network or out-of-network providers.;2018-06-05T14:06:02+00:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;in-network;In Network;Provider is contracted with the health insurance company to provide services to plan members for specific pre-negotiated rates;;;
insuranceplan-applicability;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/applicability;4.0.1;BenefitCostApplicability;Benefit cost applicability;draft;False;Whether the cost applies to in-network or out-of-network providers.;2018-06-05T14:06:02+00:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;out-of-network;Out of Network;Provider is  not contracted with the health insurance company to provide services to plan members for specific pre-negotiated rates;;;
insuranceplan-applicability;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/applicability;4.0.1;BenefitCostApplicability;Benefit cost applicability;draft;False;Whether the cost applies to in-network or out-of-network providers.;2018-06-05T14:06:02+00:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;other;Other;Other applicability;;;
