location-physical-type;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/location-physical-type;4.0.1;LocationType;Location type;draft;False;This example value set defines a set of codes that can be used to indicate the physical form of the Location.;;FHIR Project team;complete;si;Site;A collection of buildings or other locations such as a site or a campus.;;;
location-physical-type;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/location-physical-type;4.0.1;LocationType;Location type;draft;False;This example value set defines a set of codes that can be used to indicate the physical form of the Location.;;FHIR Project team;complete;bu;Building;Any Building or structure. This may contain rooms, corridors, wings, etc. It might not have walls, or a roof, but is considered a defined/allocated space.;;;
location-physical-type;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/location-physical-type;4.0.1;LocationType;Location type;draft;False;This example value set defines a set of codes that can be used to indicate the physical form of the Location.;;FHIR Project team;complete;wi;Wing;A Wing within a Building, this often contains levels, rooms and corridors.;;;
location-physical-type;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/location-physical-type;4.0.1;LocationType;Location type;draft;False;This example value set defines a set of codes that can be used to indicate the physical form of the Location.;;FHIR Project team;complete;wa;Ward;A Ward is a section of a medical facility that may contain rooms and other types of location.;;;
location-physical-type;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/location-physical-type;4.0.1;LocationType;Location type;draft;False;This example value set defines a set of codes that can be used to indicate the physical form of the Location.;;FHIR Project team;complete;lvl;Level;A Level in a multi-level Building/Structure.;;;
