nhin-purposeofuse;http://healthit.gov/nhin/purposeofuse;2.0;NHIN PurposeOfUse;;active;False;This value set is suitable for use with the provenance resource. It is derived from, but not compatible with, the HL7 v3 Purpose of use Code system.;2010-01-29;Nationwide Health Information Network (NHIN);complete;PUBLICHEALTH;Public Health;Uses and disclosures for public health activities.;;;
nhin-purposeofuse;http://healthit.gov/nhin/purposeofuse;2.0;NHIN PurposeOfUse;;active;False;This value set is suitable for use with the provenance resource. It is derived from, but not compatible with, the HL7 v3 Purpose of use Code system.;2010-01-29;Nationwide Health Information Network (NHIN);complete;ABUSE;Abuse;Disclosures about victims of abuse, neglect or domestic violence.;;;
nhin-purposeofuse;http://healthit.gov/nhin/purposeofuse;2.0;NHIN PurposeOfUse;;active;False;This value set is suitable for use with the provenance resource. It is derived from, but not compatible with, the HL7 v3 Purpose of use Code system.;2010-01-29;Nationwide Health Information Network (NHIN);complete;OVERSIGHT;Oversight;Uses and disclosures for health oversight activities.;;;
nhin-purposeofuse;http://healthit.gov/nhin/purposeofuse;2.0;NHIN PurposeOfUse;;active;False;This value set is suitable for use with the provenance resource. It is derived from, but not compatible with, the HL7 v3 Purpose of use Code system.;2010-01-29;Nationwide Health Information Network (NHIN);complete;JUDICIAL;Judicial;Disclosures for judicial and administrative proceedings.;;;
nhin-purposeofuse;http://healthit.gov/nhin/purposeofuse;2.0;NHIN PurposeOfUse;;active;False;This value set is suitable for use with the provenance resource. It is derived from, but not compatible with, the HL7 v3 Purpose of use Code system.;2010-01-29;Nationwide Health Information Network (NHIN);complete;LAW;Law Enforcement;Disclosures for law enforcement purposes.;;;
nhin-purposeofuse;http://healthit.gov/nhin/purposeofuse;2.0;NHIN PurposeOfUse;;active;False;This value set is suitable for use with the provenance resource. It is derived from, but not compatible with, the HL7 v3 Purpose of use Code system.;2010-01-29;Nationwide Health Information Network (NHIN);complete;DECEASED;Deceased;Uses and disclosures about decedents.;;;
nhin-purposeofuse;http://healthit.gov/nhin/purposeofuse;2.0;NHIN PurposeOfUse;;active;False;This value set is suitable for use with the provenance resource. It is derived from, but not compatible with, the HL7 v3 Purpose of use Code system.;2010-01-29;Nationwide Health Information Network (NHIN);complete;DONATION;Donation;Uses and disclosures for cadaveric organ,  eye or tissue donation purposes;;;
nhin-purposeofuse;http://healthit.gov/nhin/purposeofuse;2.0;NHIN PurposeOfUse;;active;False;This value set is suitable for use with the provenance resource. It is derived from, but not compatible with, the HL7 v3 Purpose of use Code system.;2010-01-29;Nationwide Health Information Network (NHIN);complete;RESEARCH;Research;Uses and disclosures for research purposes.;;;
nhin-purposeofuse;http://healthit.gov/nhin/purposeofuse;2.0;NHIN PurposeOfUse;;active;False;This value set is suitable for use with the provenance resource. It is derived from, but not compatible with, the HL7 v3 Purpose of use Code system.;2010-01-29;Nationwide Health Information Network (NHIN);complete;THREAT;Threat;Uses and disclosures to avert a serious threat to health or safety.;;;
nhin-purposeofuse;http://healthit.gov/nhin/purposeofuse;2.0;NHIN PurposeOfUse;;active;False;This value set is suitable for use with the provenance resource. It is derived from, but not compatible with, the HL7 v3 Purpose of use Code system.;2010-01-29;Nationwide Health Information Network (NHIN);complete;GOVERNMENT;Government;Uses and disclosures for specialized government functions.;;;
nhin-purposeofuse;http://healthit.gov/nhin/purposeofuse;2.0;NHIN PurposeOfUse;;active;False;This value set is suitable for use with the provenance resource. It is derived from, but not compatible with, the HL7 v3 Purpose of use Code system.;2010-01-29;Nationwide Health Information Network (NHIN);complete;WORKERSCOMP;Worker's Comp;Disclosures for workers' compensation.;;;
nhin-purposeofuse;http://healthit.gov/nhin/purposeofuse;2.0;NHIN PurposeOfUse;;active;False;This value set is suitable for use with the provenance resource. It is derived from, but not compatible with, the HL7 v3 Purpose of use Code system.;2010-01-29;Nationwide Health Information Network (NHIN);complete;COVERAGE;Coverage;Disclosures for insurance or disability coverage determination;;;
nhin-purposeofuse;http://healthit.gov/nhin/purposeofuse;2.0;NHIN PurposeOfUse;;active;False;This value set is suitable for use with the provenance resource. It is derived from, but not compatible with, the HL7 v3 Purpose of use Code system.;2010-01-29;Nationwide Health Information Network (NHIN);complete;REQUEST;Request;Request of the Individual;;;
note-type;http://hl7.org/fhir/note-type;4.0.1;NoteType;NoteType;draft;False;The presentation types of notes.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;;complete;display;Display;Display the note.;;;
note-type;http://hl7.org/fhir/note-type;4.0.1;NoteType;NoteType;draft;False;The presentation types of notes.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;;complete;print;Print (Form);Print the note on the form.;;;
note-type;http://hl7.org/fhir/note-type;4.0.1;NoteType;NoteType;draft;False;The presentation types of notes.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;;complete;printoper;Print (Operator);Print the note for the operator.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;1;Patient;This object is the patient that is the subject of care related to this event.  It is identifiable by patient ID or equivalent.  The patient may be either human or animal.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;2;Location;This is a location identified as related to the event.  This is usually the location where the event took place.  Note that for shipping, the usual events are arrival at a location or departure from a location.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;3;Report;This object is any kind of persistent document created as a result of the event.  This could be a paper report, film, electronic report, DICOM Study, etc.  Issues related to medical records life cycle management are conveyed elsewhere.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;4;Domain Resource;A logical object related to a health record event.  This is any healthcare  specific resource (object) not restricted to FHIR defined Resources.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;5;Master file;This is any configurable file used to control creation of documents.  Examples include the objects maintained by the HL7 Master File transactions, Value Sets, etc.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;6;User;A human participant not otherwise identified by some other category.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;7;List;(deprecated).;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;8;Doctor;Typically, a licensed person who is providing or performing care related to the event, generally a physician.   The key distinction between doctor and practitioner is with regards to their role, not the licensing.  The doctor is the human who actually performed the work.  The practitioner is the human or organization that is responsible for the work.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;9;Subscriber;A person or system that is being notified as part of the event.  This is relevant in situations where automated systems provide notifications to other parties when an event took place.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;10;Guarantor;Insurance company, or any other organization who accepts responsibility for paying for the healthcare event.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;11;Security User Entity;A person or active system object involved in the event with a security role.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;12;Security User Group;A person or system object involved in the event with the authority to modify security roles of other objects.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;13;Security Resource;A passive object, such as a role table, that is relevant to the event.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;14;Security Granularity Definition;(deprecated)  Relevant to certain RBAC security methodologies.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;15;Practitioner;Any person or organization responsible for providing care.  This encompasses all forms of care, licensed or otherwise, and all sorts of teams and care groups. Note the distinction between practitioner and the doctor that actually provided the care to the patient.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;16;Data Destination;The source or destination for data transfer, when it does not match some other role.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;17;Data Repository;A source or destination for data transfer that acts as an archive, database, or similar role.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;18;Schedule;An object that holds schedule information.  This could be an appointment book, availability information, etc.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;19;Customer;An organization or person that is the recipient of services.  This could be an organization that is buying services for a patient, or a person that is buying services for an animal.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;20;Job;"An order, task, work item, procedure step, or other description of work to be performed; e.g. a particular instance of an MPPS.";;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;21;Job Stream;"A list of jobs or a system that provides lists of jobs; e.g. an MWL SCP.";;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;22;Table;(Deprecated).;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;23;Routing Criteria;An object that specifies or controls the routing or delivery of items.  For example, a distribution list is the routing criteria for mail.  The items delivered may be documents, jobs, or other objects.;;;
object-role;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/object-role;4.0.1;AuditEventEntityRole;AuditEventEntityRole;draft;False;Code representing the role the entity played in the audit event.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;24;Query;The contents of a query.  This is used to capture the contents of any kind of query.  For security surveillance purposes knowing the queries being made is very important.;;;
observation-category;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-category;4.0.1;ObservationCategoryCodes;Observation Category Codes;draft;False;Observation Category codes.;;FHIR Project team;complete;social-history;Social History;Social History Observations define the patient's occupational, personal (e.g., lifestyle), social, familial, and environmental history and health risk factors that may impact the patient's health.;;;
observation-category;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-category;4.0.1;ObservationCategoryCodes;Observation Category Codes;draft;False;Observation Category codes.;;FHIR Project team;complete;vital-signs;Vital Signs; Clinical observations measure the body's basic functions such as blood pressure, heart rate, respiratory rate, height, weight, body mass index, head circumference, pulse oximetry, temperature, and body surface area.;;;
observation-category;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-category;4.0.1;ObservationCategoryCodes;Observation Category Codes;draft;False;Observation Category codes.;;FHIR Project team;complete;imaging;Imaging;Observations generated by imaging. The scope includes observations regarding plain x-ray, ultrasound, CT, MRI, angiography, echocardiography, and nuclear medicine.;;;
observation-category;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-category;4.0.1;ObservationCategoryCodes;Observation Category Codes;draft;False;Observation Category codes.;;FHIR Project team;complete;laboratory;Laboratory;The results of observations generated by laboratories.  Laboratory results are typically generated by laboratories providing analytic services in areas such as chemistry, hematology, serology, histology, cytology, anatomic pathology (including digital pathology), microbiology, and/or virology. These observations are based on analysis of specimens obtained from the patient and submitted to the laboratory.;;;
observation-category;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-category;4.0.1;ObservationCategoryCodes;Observation Category Codes;draft;False;Observation Category codes.;;FHIR Project team;complete;procedure;Procedure;Observations generated by other procedures.  This category includes observations resulting from interventional and non-interventional procedures excluding laboratory and imaging (e.g., cardiology catheterization, endoscopy, electrodiagnostics, etc.).  Procedure results are typically generated by a clinician to provide more granular information about component observations made during a procedure.  An example would be when a gastroenterologist reports the size of a polyp observed during a colonoscopy.;;;
observation-category;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-category;4.0.1;ObservationCategoryCodes;Observation Category Codes;draft;False;Observation Category codes.;;FHIR Project team;complete;survey;Survey;Assessment tool/survey instrument observations (e.g., Apgar Scores, Montreal Cognitive Assessment (MoCA)).;;;
observation-category;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-category;4.0.1;ObservationCategoryCodes;Observation Category Codes;draft;False;Observation Category codes.;;FHIR Project team;complete;exam;Exam;Observations generated by physical exam findings including direct observations made by a clinician and use of simple instruments and the result of simple maneuvers performed directly on the patient's body.;;;
observation-category;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-category;4.0.1;ObservationCategoryCodes;Observation Category Codes;draft;False;Observation Category codes.;;FHIR Project team;complete;therapy;Therapy;Observations generated by non-interventional treatment protocols (e.g. occupational, physical, radiation, nutritional and medication therapy);;;
observation-category;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-category;4.0.1;ObservationCategoryCodes;Observation Category Codes;draft;False;Observation Category codes.;;FHIR Project team;complete;activity;Activity;Observations that measure or record any bodily activity that enhances or maintains physical fitness and overall health and wellness.  Not under direct supervision of practitioner such as a physical therapist. (e.g., laps swum, steps, sleep data);;;
observation-range-category;http://hl7.org/fhir/observation-range-category;4.0.1;ObservationRangeCategory;ObservationRangeCategory;draft;False;Codes identifying the category of observation range.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;reference;reference range;Reference (Normal) Range for Ordinal and Continuous Observations.;;;
observation-range-category;http://hl7.org/fhir/observation-range-category;4.0.1;ObservationRangeCategory;ObservationRangeCategory;draft;False;Codes identifying the category of observation range.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;critical;critical range;Critical Range for Ordinal and Continuous Observations.;;;
observation-range-category;http://hl7.org/fhir/observation-range-category;4.0.1;ObservationRangeCategory;ObservationRangeCategory;draft;False;Codes identifying the category of observation range.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;absolute;absolute range;Absolute Range for Ordinal and Continuous Observations. Results outside this range are not possible.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;average;Average;The [mean](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arithmetic_mean) of N measurements over the stated period.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;maximum;Maximum;The [maximum](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maximal_element) value of N measurements over the stated period.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;minimum;Minimum;The [minimum](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minimal_element) value of N measurements over the stated period.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;count;Count;The [number] of valid measurements over the stated period that contributed to the other statistical outputs.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;total-count;Total Count;The total [number] of valid measurements over the stated period, including observations that were ignored because they did not contain valid result values.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;median;Median;The [median](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Median) of N measurements over the stated period.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;std-dev;Standard Deviation;The [standard deviation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_deviation) of N measurements over the stated period.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;sum;Sum;The [sum](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summation) of N measurements over the stated period.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;variance;Variance;The [variance](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Variance) of N measurements over the stated period.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;20-percent;20th Percentile;The 20th [Percentile](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Percentile) of N measurements over the stated period.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;80-percent;80th Percentile;The 80th [Percentile](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Percentile) of N measurements over the stated period.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;4-lower;Lower Quartile;The lower [Quartile](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quartile) Boundary of N measurements over the stated period.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;4-upper;Upper Quartile;The upper [Quartile](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quartile) Boundary of N measurements over the stated period.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;4-dev;Quartile Deviation;The difference between the upper and lower [Quartiles](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quartile) is called the Interquartile range. (IQR = Q3-Q1) Quartile deviation or Semi-interquartile range is one-half the difference between the first and the third quartiles.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;5-1;1st Quintile;The lowest of four values that divide the N measurements into a frequency distribution of five classes with each containing one fifth of the total population.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;5-2;2nd Quintile;The second of four values that divide the N measurements into a frequency distribution of five classes with each containing one fifth of the total population.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;5-3;3rd Quintile;The third of four values that divide the N measurements into a frequency distribution of five classes with each containing one fifth of the total population.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;5-4;4th Quintile;The fourth of four values that divide the N measurements into a frequency distribution of five classes with each containing one fifth of the total population.;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;skew;Skew;Skewness is a measure of the asymmetry of the probability distribution of a real-valued random variable about its mean. The skewness value can be positive or negative, or even undefined.  Source: [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skewness).;;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;kurtosis;Kurtosis;"Kurtosis  is a measure of the ""tailedness"" of the probability distribution of a real-valued random variable.   Source: [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kurtosis).";;;
observation-statistics;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-statistics;4.0.1;StatisticsCode;StatisticsCode;draft;False;"The statistical operation parameter -""statistic"" codes.";2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;regression;Regression;Linear regression is an approach for modeling two-dimensional sample points with one independent variable and one dependent variable (conventionally, the x and y coordinates in a Cartesian coordinate system) and finds a linear function (a non-vertical straight line) that, as accurately as possible, predicts the dependent variable values as a function of the independent variables. Source: [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simple_linear_regression)  This Statistic code will return both a gradient and an intercept value.;;;
observation-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/observation-status;4.0.1;ObservationStatus;ObservationStatus;active;False;Codes providing the status of an observation.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;registered;Registered;The existence of the observation is registered, but there is no result yet available.;;;
observation-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/observation-status;4.0.1;ObservationStatus;ObservationStatus;active;False;Codes providing the status of an observation.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;preliminary;Preliminary;This is an initial or interim observation: data may be incomplete or unverified.;;;
observation-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/observation-status;4.0.1;ObservationStatus;ObservationStatus;active;False;Codes providing the status of an observation.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;final;Final;"The observation is complete and there are no further actions needed. Additional information such ""released"", ""signed"", etc would be represented using [Provenance](provenance.html) which provides not only the act but also the actors and dates and other related data. These act states would be associated with an observation status of `preliminary` until they are all completed and then a status of `final` would be applied.";;;
observation-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/observation-status;4.0.1;ObservationStatus;ObservationStatus;active;False;Codes providing the status of an observation.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;amended;Amended;Subsequent to being Final, the observation has been modified subsequent.  This includes updates/new information and corrections.;corrected;Corrected;Subsequent to being Final, the observation has been modified to correct an error in the test result.
observation-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/observation-status;4.0.1;ObservationStatus;ObservationStatus;active;False;Codes providing the status of an observation.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;cancelled;Cancelled;"The observation is unavailable because the measurement was not started or not completed (also sometimes called ""aborted"").";;;
observation-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/observation-status;4.0.1;ObservationStatus;ObservationStatus;active;False;Codes providing the status of an observation.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;entered-in-error;Entered in Error;"The observation has been withdrawn following previous final release.  This electronic record should never have existed, though it is possible that real-world decisions were based on it. (If real-world activity has occurred, the status should be ""cancelled"" rather than ""entered-in-error"".).";;;
observation-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/observation-status;4.0.1;ObservationStatus;ObservationStatus;active;False;Codes providing the status of an observation.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;unknown;Unknown;"The authoring/source system does not know which of the status values currently applies for this observation. Note: This concept is not to be used for ""other"" - one of the listed statuses is presumed to apply, but the authoring/source system does not know which.";;;
