questionnaire-item-control;http://hl7.org/fhir/questionnaire-item-control;4.0.1;QuestionnaireItemUIControlCodes;Questionnaire Item UI Control Codes;draft;False;Starter set of user interface control/display mechanisms that might be used when rendering an item in a questionnaire.;;HL7 International - Patient Care WG;complete;text;;UI controls relevant to rendering questionnaire text items;prompt;Prompt;Text is displayed immediately below or within the answer-entry area of the containing question item (typically as a guide for what to enter)
questionnaire-item-control;http://hl7.org/fhir/questionnaire-item-control;4.0.1;QuestionnaireItemUIControlCodes;Questionnaire Item UI Control Codes;draft;False;Starter set of user interface control/display mechanisms that might be used when rendering an item in a questionnaire.;;HL7 International - Patient Care WG;complete;text;;UI controls relevant to rendering questionnaire text items;unit;Unit;Text is displayed adjacent (horizontally or vertically) to the answer space for the parent question, typically to indicate a unit of measure
questionnaire-item-control;http://hl7.org/fhir/questionnaire-item-control;4.0.1;QuestionnaireItemUIControlCodes;Questionnaire Item UI Control Codes;draft;False;Starter set of user interface control/display mechanisms that might be used when rendering an item in a questionnaire.;;HL7 International - Patient Care WG;complete;text;;UI controls relevant to rendering questionnaire text items;lower;Lower-bound;Text is displayed to the left of the set of answer choices or a scaling control for the parent question item to indicate the meaning of the 'lower' bound.  E.g. 'Strongly disagree'
