responding, withdrawal, non-compliance and/or adverse event.";;;
research-subject-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/research-subject-status;4.0.1;ResearchSubjectStatus;ResearchSubjectStatus;draft;False;Indicates the progression of a study subject through a study.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;on-study;On-study;A person that is enrolled or registered on a study.;;;
research-subject-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/research-subject-status;4.0.1;ResearchSubjectStatus;ResearchSubjectStatus;draft;False;Indicates the progression of a study subject through a study.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;on-study-intervention;On-study-intervention;The person is receiving the treatment or participating in an activity (e.g. yoga, diet, etc.) that the study is evaluating.;;;
research-subject-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/research-subject-status;4.0.1;ResearchSubjectStatus;ResearchSubjectStatus;draft;False;Indicates the progression of a study subject through a study.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;on-study-observation;On-study-observation;"The subject is being evaluated via tests and assessments according to the study calendar, but is not receiving any intervention. Note that this state is study-dependent and might not exist in all studies.  A synonym for this is ""short-term follow-up"".";;;
research-subject-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/research-subject-status;4.0.1;ResearchSubjectStatus;ResearchSubjectStatus;draft;False;Indicates the progression of a study subject through a study.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;pending-on-study;Pending on-study;A person is pre-registered for a study.;;;
research-subject-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/research-subject-status;4.0.1;ResearchSubjectStatus;ResearchSubjectStatus;draft;False;Indicates the progression of a study subject through a study.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;potential-candidate;Potential Candidate;A person that is potentially eligible for participation in the study.;;;
research-subject-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/research-subject-status;4.0.1;ResearchSubjectStatus;ResearchSubjectStatus;draft;False;Indicates the progression of a study subject through a study.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;screening;Screening;A person who is being evaluated for eligibility for a study.;;;
research-subject-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/research-subject-status;4.0.1;ResearchSubjectStatus;ResearchSubjectStatus;draft;False;Indicates the progression of a study subject through a study.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;withdrawn;Withdrawn;The person has withdrawn their participation in the study before registration.;;;
resource-aggregation-mode;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-aggregation-mode;4.0.1;AggregationMode;AggregationMode;active;False;How resource references can be aggregated.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;contained;Contained;The reference is a local reference to a contained resource.;;;
resource-aggregation-mode;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-aggregation-mode;4.0.1;AggregationMode;AggregationMode;active;False;How resource references can be aggregated.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;referenced;Referenced;The reference to a resource that has to be resolved externally to the resource that includes the reference.;bundled;Bundled;The resource the reference points to will be found in the same bundle as the resource that includes the reference.
resource-security-category;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/resource-security-category;4.0.1;ResourceSecurityCategory;ResourceSecurityCategory;draft;False;Provides general guidance around the kind of access Control to Read, Search, Create, Update, or Delete a resource.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;anonymous;Anonymous READ Access Resource;These resources tend to not contain any individual data, or business sensitive data. Most often these Resources will be available for anonymous access, meaning there is no access control based on the user or system requesting. However these Resources do tend to contain important information that must be authenticated back to the source publishing them, and protected from integrity failures in communication. For this reason server authenticated https (TLS) is recommended to provide authentication of the server and integrity protection in transit. This is normal web-server use of https.;;;
resource-security-category;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/resource-security-category;4.0.1;ResourceSecurityCategory;ResourceSecurityCategory;draft;False;Provides general guidance around the kind of access Control to Read, Search, Create, Update, or Delete a resource.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;business;Business Sensitive Resource;These Resources tend to not contain any individual data, but do have data that describe business or service sensitive data. The use of the term Business is not intended to only mean an incorporated business, but rather the more broad concept of an organization, location, or other group that is not identifable as individuals. Often these resources will require some for of client authentication to assure that only authorized access is given. The client access control may be to individuals, or may be to system identity. For this purpose possible client authentication methods such as: mutual-authenticated-TLS, APIKey, App signed JWT, or App OAuth client-id JWT For example: a App that uses a Business protected Provider Directory to determine other business endpoint details.;;;
resource-security-category;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/resource-security-category;4.0.1;ResourceSecurityCategory;ResourceSecurityCategory;draft;False;Provides general guidance around the kind of access Control to Read, Search, Create, Update, or Delete a resource.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;individual;Individual Sensitive Resource;These Resources do NOT contain Patient data, but do contain individual information about other participants. These other individuals are Practitioners, PractionerRole, CareTeam, or other users. These identities are needed to enable the practice of healthcare. These identities are identities under general privacy regulations, and thus must consider Privacy risk. Often access to these other identities are covered by business relationships. For this purpose access to these Resources will tend to be Role specific using methods such as RBAC or ABAC.;;;
resource-security-category;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/resource-security-category;4.0.1;ResourceSecurityCategory;ResourceSecurityCategory;draft;False;Provides general guidance around the kind of access Control to Read, Search, Create, Update, or Delete a resource.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;patient;Patient Sensitive;These Resources make up the bulk of FHIR and therefore are the most commonly understood. These Resources contain highly sesitive health information, or are closely linked to highly sensitive health information. These Resources will often use the security labels to differentiate various confidentiality levels within this broad group of Patient Sensitive data. Access to these Resources often requires a declared Purpose Of Use. Access to these Resources is often controlled by a Privacy Consent.;;;
resource-security-category;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/resource-security-category;4.0.1;ResourceSecurityCategory;ResourceSecurityCategory;draft;False;Provides general guidance around the kind of access Control to Read, Search, Create, Update, or Delete a resource.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;not-classified;Not classified;Some Resources can be used for a wide scope of use-cases that span very sensitive to very non-sensitive. These Resources do not fall into any of the above classifications, as their sensitivity is highly variable. These Resources will need special handling. These Resources often contain metadata that describes the content in a way that can be used for Access Control decisions.;;;
resource-slicing-rules;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-slicing-rules;4.0.1;SlicingRules;SlicingRules;active;False;How slices are interpreted when evaluating an instance.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;closed;Closed;No additional content is allowed other than that described by the slices in this profile.;;;
resource-slicing-rules;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-slicing-rules;4.0.1;SlicingRules;SlicingRules;active;False;How slices are interpreted when evaluating an instance.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;open;Open;Additional content is allowed anywhere in the list.;;;
resource-slicing-rules;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-slicing-rules;4.0.1;SlicingRules;SlicingRules;active;False;How slices are interpreted when evaluating an instance.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;openAtEnd;Open at End;Additional content is allowed, but only at the end of the list. Note that using this requires that the slices be ordered, which makes it hard to share uses. This should only be done where absolutely required.;;;
resource-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-status;4.0.1;Canonical Status Codes for FHIR Resources;;draft;;The master set of status codes used throughout FHIR. All status codes are mapped to one of these codes.;;FHIR Project;complete;error;error;The resource was created in error, and should not be treated as valid (note: in many cases, for various data integrity related reasons, the information cannot be removed from the record);;;
resource-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-status;4.0.1;Canonical Status Codes for FHIR Resources;;draft;;The master set of status codes used throughout FHIR. All status codes are mapped to one of these codes.;;FHIR Project;complete;proposed;proposed;The resource describes an action or plan that is proposed, and not yet approved by the participants;;;
resource-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-status;4.0.1;Canonical Status Codes for FHIR Resources;;draft;;The master set of status codes used throughout FHIR. All status codes are mapped to one of these codes.;;FHIR Project;complete;planned;planned;The resource describes a course of action that is planned and agreed/approved, but at the time of recording was still future;;;
resource-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-status;4.0.1;Canonical Status Codes for FHIR Resources;;draft;;The master set of status codes used throughout FHIR. All status codes are mapped to one of these codes.;;FHIR Project;complete;draft;draft;The information in the resource is still being prepared and edited;;;
resource-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-status;4.0.1;Canonical Status Codes for FHIR Resources;;draft;;The master set of status codes used throughout FHIR. All status codes are mapped to one of these codes.;;FHIR Project;complete;requested;requested;A fulfiller has been asked to perform this action, but it has not yet occurred;;;
resource-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-status;4.0.1;Canonical Status Codes for FHIR Resources;;draft;;The master set of status codes used throughout FHIR. All status codes are mapped to one of these codes.;;FHIR Project;complete;received;received;The fulfiller has received the request, but not yet agreed to carry out the action;;;
resource-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-status;4.0.1;Canonical Status Codes for FHIR Resources;;draft;;The master set of status codes used throughout FHIR. All status codes are mapped to one of these codes.;;FHIR Project;complete;declined;declined;The fulfiller chose not to perform the action;;;
resource-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-status;4.0.1;Canonical Status Codes for FHIR Resources;;draft;;The master set of status codes used throughout FHIR. All status codes are mapped to one of these codes.;;FHIR Project;complete;accepted;accepted;The fulfiller has decided to perform the action, and plans are in train to do this in the future;;;
resource-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-status;4.0.1;Canonical Status Codes for FHIR Resources;;draft;;The master set of status codes used throughout FHIR. All status codes are mapped to one of these codes.;;FHIR Project;complete;arrived;arrived;The pre-conditions for the action are all fulfilled, and it is imminent;;;
resource-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-status;4.0.1;Canonical Status Codes for FHIR Resources;;draft;;The master set of status codes used throughout FHIR. All status codes are mapped to one of these codes.;;FHIR Project;complete;active;active;The resource describes information that is currently valid or a process that is presently occuring;;;
resource-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-status;4.0.1;Canonical Status Codes for FHIR Resources;;draft;;The master set of status codes used throughout FHIR. All status codes are mapped to one of these codes.;;FHIR Project;complete;suspended;suspended;The process described/requested in this resource has been halted for some reason;;;
resource-status;http://hl7.org/fhir/resource-status;4.0.1;Canonical Status Codes for FHIR Resources;;draft;;The master set of status codes used throughout FHIR. All status codes are mapped to one of these codes.;;FHIR Project;complete;failed;failed;The process described/requested in the resource could not be completed, and no further action is planned;;;
