unknown-content-code;http://hl7.org/fhir/unknown-content-code;4.0.1;UnknownContentCode;UnknownContentCode;draft;False;A code that indicates whether an application accepts unknown elements or extensions when reading resources.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;no;Neither Elements or Extensions;The application does not accept either unknown elements or extensions.;;;
unknown-content-code;http://hl7.org/fhir/unknown-content-code;4.0.1;UnknownContentCode;UnknownContentCode;draft;False;A code that indicates whether an application accepts unknown elements or extensions when reading resources.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;extensions;Unknown Extensions;The application accepts unknown extensions, but not unknown elements.;;;
unknown-content-code;http://hl7.org/fhir/unknown-content-code;4.0.1;UnknownContentCode;UnknownContentCode;draft;False;A code that indicates whether an application accepts unknown elements or extensions when reading resources.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;elements;Unknown Elements;The application accepts unknown elements, but not unknown extensions.;;;
unknown-content-code;http://hl7.org/fhir/unknown-content-code;4.0.1;UnknownContentCode;UnknownContentCode;draft;False;A code that indicates whether an application accepts unknown elements or extensions when reading resources.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;both;Unknown Elements and Extensions;The application accepts unknown elements and extensions.;;;
usage-context-type;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/usage-context-type;4.0.1;UsageContextType;UsageContextType;draft;False;A code that specifies a type of context being specified by a usage context.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;gender;Gender;The gender of the patient. For this context type, appropriate values can be found in the http://hl7.org/fhir/ValueSet/administrative-gender value set.;;;
usage-context-type;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/usage-context-type;4.0.1;UsageContextType;UsageContextType;draft;False;A code that specifies a type of context being specified by a usage context.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;age;Age Range;The age of the patient. For this context type, the value could be a range that specifies the applicable ages or a code from an appropriate value set such as the MeSH value set http://terminology.hl7.org/ValueSet/v3-AgeGroupObservationValue.;;;
usage-context-type;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/usage-context-type;4.0.1;UsageContextType;UsageContextType;draft;False;A code that specifies a type of context being specified by a usage context.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;focus;Clinical Focus;The clinical concept(s) addressed by the artifact. For example, disease, diagnostic test interpretation, medication ordering as in http://hl7.org/fhir/ValueSet/condition-code.;;;
usage-context-type;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/usage-context-type;4.0.1;UsageContextType;UsageContextType;draft;False;A code that specifies a type of context being specified by a usage context.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;user;User Type;The clinical specialty of the context in which the patient is being treated - For example, PCP, Patient, Cardiologist, Behavioral Professional, Oral Health Professional, Prescriber, etc... taken from a specialty value set such as the NUCC Health Care provider taxonomy value set http://hl7.org/fhir/ValueSet/provider-taxonomy.;;;
usage-context-type;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/usage-context-type;4.0.1;UsageContextType;UsageContextType;draft;False;A code that specifies a type of context being specified by a usage context.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;workflow;Workflow Setting;The settings in which the artifact is intended for use. For example, admission, pre-op, etc. For example, the ActEncounterCode value set http://terminology.hl7.org/ValueSet/v3-ActEncounterCode.;;;
usage-context-type;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/usage-context-type;4.0.1;UsageContextType;UsageContextType;draft;False;A code that specifies a type of context being specified by a usage context.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;task;Workflow Task;The context for the clinical task(s) represented by this artifact. For example, this could be any task context represented by the HL7 ActTaskCode value set http://terminology.hl7.org/ValueSet/v3-ActTaskCode. General categories include: order entry, patient documentation and patient information review.;;;
usage-context-type;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/usage-context-type;4.0.1;UsageContextType;UsageContextType;draft;False;A code that specifies a type of context being specified by a usage context.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;venue;Clinical Venue;The venue in which an artifact could be used. For example, Outpatient, Inpatient, Home, Nursing home. The code value may originate from the HL7 ServiceDeliveryLocationRoleType value set (http://terminology.hl7.org/ValueSet/v3-ServiceDeliveryLocationRoleType).;;;
usage-context-type;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/usage-context-type;4.0.1;UsageContextType;UsageContextType;draft;False;A code that specifies a type of context being specified by a usage context.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;species;Species;The species to which an artifact applies. For example, SNOMED - 387961004 | Kingdom Animalia (organism).;;;
usage-context-type;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/usage-context-type;4.0.1;UsageContextType;UsageContextType;draft;False;A code that specifies a type of context being specified by a usage context.;2019-11-01T09:29:23+11:00;HL7 (FHIR Project);complete;program;Program;A program/project of work for which this artifact is applicable.;;;
