v3-ActRelationshipCheckpoint;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipCheckpoint;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipCheckpoint;v3 Code System ActRelationshipCheckpoint;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;B;beginning;Condition is tested every time before execution of the service (WHILE condition DO service).;;;
v3-ActRelationshipCheckpoint;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipCheckpoint;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipCheckpoint;v3 Code System ActRelationshipCheckpoint;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;E;end;Condition is tested at the end of a repeated service execution.  The service is repeated only if the condition is true (DO service WHILE condition).;;;
v3-ActRelationshipCheckpoint;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipCheckpoint;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipCheckpoint;v3 Code System ActRelationshipCheckpoint;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;S;entry;Condition is tested once before the service is executed (IF condition THEN service).;;;
v3-ActRelationshipCheckpoint;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipCheckpoint;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipCheckpoint;v3 Code System ActRelationshipCheckpoint;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;T;through;Condition must be true throughout the execution and the service is interrupted (asynchronously) as soon as the condition turns false (asynchronous WHILE loop).  The service must be interruptible.;;;
v3-ActRelationshipCheckpoint;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipCheckpoint;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipCheckpoint;v3 Code System ActRelationshipCheckpoint;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;X;exit;Condition is a loop checkpoint, i.e. it is a step of an activity plan and, if negative causes the containing loop to exit.;;;
v3-ActRelationshipJoin;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipJoin;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipJoin;v3 Code System ActRelationshipJoin;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;D;detached;Detach this branch from the other branches so it will not be resynchronized with the other branches.;;;
v3-ActRelationshipJoin;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipJoin;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipJoin;v3 Code System ActRelationshipJoin;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;K;kill;When all other concurrent branches are terminated, interrupt and discontinue this branch.;;;
v3-ActRelationshipJoin;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipJoin;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipJoin;v3 Code System ActRelationshipJoin;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;W;wait;Wait for this branch to terminate.;;;
v3-ActRelationshipJoin;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipJoin;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipJoin;v3 Code System ActRelationshipJoin;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;X;exclusive wait;Wait for any one of the branches in the set of exclusive wait branches to terminate, then discontinue all the other exclusive wait branches.;;;
v3-ActRelationshipSplit;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipSplit;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipSplit;v3 Code System ActRelationshipSplit;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;E1;exclusive try once;"The pre-condition associated with the branch is evaluated once and if true the branch may be entered. All other exclusive branches compete with each other and only one will be selected. This implements a COND, IF and CASE conditionals, or ""XOR-split."" The order in which the branches are considered may be specified in the priorityNumber attribute.";;;
v3-ActRelationshipSplit;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipSplit;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipSplit;v3 Code System ActRelationshipSplit;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;EW;exclusive wait;A branch is selected as soon as the pre-condition associated with the branch evaluates to true.  If the condition is false, the branch may be entered later, when the condition turns true.  All other exclusive branches compete with each other and only one will be selected.  Each waiting branch executes in parallel with the default join code wait  (see below). The order in which the branches are considered may be specified in the Service_relationship.priority_nmb.;;;
v3-ActRelationshipSplit;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipSplit;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipSplit;v3 Code System ActRelationshipSplit;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;I1;inclusive try once;A branch is executed if its associated preconditions permit. If associated preconditions do not permit, the branch is dropped.  Inclusive branches are not suppressed and do not suppress other branches.;;;
v3-ActRelationshipSplit;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipSplit;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipSplit;v3 Code System ActRelationshipSplit;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;IW;inclusive wait;A branch is executed as soon as its associated conditions permit.  If the condition is false, the branch may be entered later, when the condition turns true.  Inclusive branches are not suppressed and do not suppress other branches.  Each waiting branch executes in parallel with the default join code wait  (see below).;;;
v3-ActRelationshipSubset;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipSubset;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipSubset;v3 Code System ActRelationshipSubset;active;False; <ns1:p>Used to indicate that the target of the relationship will be a filtered subset of the total related set of targets.</ns1:p><ns1:p>Used when there is a need to limit the number of components to the first, the last, the next, the total, the average or some other filtered or calculated subset.</ns1:p>;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;_ParticipationSubset;ParticipationSubset;"Used to indicate that the participation is a filtered subset of the total participations of the same type owned by the Act.

                        Used when there is a need to limit the participations to the first, the last, the next or some other filtered subset.";FUTURE;expected future;An occurrence that is scheduled to occur in the future. An Act whose effective time is greater than 'now', where 'now' is the time the instance is authored.
v3-ActRelationshipSubset;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipSubset;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipSubset;v3 Code System ActRelationshipSubset;active;False; <ns1:p>Used to indicate that the target of the relationship will be a filtered subset of the total related set of targets.</ns1:p><ns1:p>Used when there is a need to limit the number of components to the first, the last, the next, the total, the average or some other filtered or calculated subset.</ns1:p>;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;FUTURE;expected future;An occurrence that is scheduled to occur in the future. An Act whose effective time is greater than 'now', where 'now' is the time the instance is authored.;FUTSUM;future summary;Represents a 'summary' of all acts that are scheduled to occur in the future (whose effective time is greater than 'now' where is the time the instance is authored.). The effectiveTime represents the outer boundary of all occurrences, repeatNumber represents the total number of repetitions, etc.
v3-ActRelationshipSubset;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipSubset;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipSubset;v3 Code System ActRelationshipSubset;active;False; <ns1:p>Used to indicate that the target of the relationship will be a filtered subset of the total related set of targets.</ns1:p><ns1:p>Used when there is a need to limit the number of components to the first, the last, the next, the total, the average or some other filtered or calculated subset.</ns1:p>;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;FUTURE;expected future;An occurrence that is scheduled to occur in the future. An Act whose effective time is greater than 'now', where 'now' is the time the instance is authored.;LAST;expected last;Restricted to the latest known occurrence that is scheduled to occur. The Act with the highest known effective time.
v3-ActRelationshipSubset;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipSubset;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipSubset;v3 Code System ActRelationshipSubset;active;False; <ns1:p>Used to indicate that the target of the relationship will be a filtered subset of the total related set of targets.</ns1:p><ns1:p>Used when there is a need to limit the number of components to the first, the last, the next, the total, the average or some other filtered or calculated subset.</ns1:p>;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;FUTURE;expected future;An occurrence that is scheduled to occur in the future. An Act whose effective time is greater than 'now', where 'now' is the time the instance is authored.;NEXT;expected next;Restricted to the nearest recent known occurrence scheduled to occur in the future. The Act with the lowest effective time, still greater than 'now'. ('now' is the time the instance is authored.)
v3-ActRelationshipSubset;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipSubset;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipSubset;v3 Code System ActRelationshipSubset;active;False; <ns1:p>Used to indicate that the target of the relationship will be a filtered subset of the total related set of targets.</ns1:p><ns1:p>Used when there is a need to limit the number of components to the first, the last, the next, the total, the average or some other filtered or calculated subset.</ns1:p>;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;_ParticipationSubset;ParticipationSubset;"Used to indicate that the participation is a filtered subset of the total participations of the same type owned by the Act.

                        Used when there is a need to limit the participations to the first, the last, the next or some other filtered subset.";PAST;previous;An occurrence that occurred or was scheduled to occur in the past. An Act whose effective time is less than 'now'. ('now' is the time the instance is authored.)
v3-ActRelationshipSubset;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipSubset;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipSubset;v3 Code System ActRelationshipSubset;active;False; <ns1:p>Used to indicate that the target of the relationship will be a filtered subset of the total related set of targets.</ns1:p><ns1:p>Used when there is a need to limit the number of components to the first, the last, the next, the total, the average or some other filtered or calculated subset.</ns1:p>;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;PAST;previous;An occurrence that occurred or was scheduled to occur in the past. An Act whose effective time is less than 'now'. ('now' is the time the instance is authored.);FIRST;first known;Restricted to the earliest known occurrence that occurred or was scheduled to occur in the past. The Act with the lowest effective time. ('now' is the time the instance is authored.)
v3-ActRelationshipSubset;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipSubset;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipSubset;v3 Code System ActRelationshipSubset;active;False; <ns1:p>Used to indicate that the target of the relationship will be a filtered subset of the total related set of targets.</ns1:p><ns1:p>Used when there is a need to limit the number of components to the first, the last, the next, the total, the average or some other filtered or calculated subset.</ns1:p>;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;PAST;previous;An occurrence that occurred or was scheduled to occur in the past. An Act whose effective time is less than 'now'. ('now' is the time the instance is authored.);PREVSUM;previous summary;Represents a 'summary' of all acts that previously occurred or were scheduled to occur. The effectiveTime represents the outer boundary of all occurrences, repeatNumber represents the total number of repetitions, etc. ('now' is the time the instance is authored.)
v3-ActRelationshipSubset;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipSubset;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipSubset;v3 Code System ActRelationshipSubset;active;False; <ns1:p>Used to indicate that the target of the relationship will be a filtered subset of the total related set of targets.</ns1:p><ns1:p>Used when there is a need to limit the number of components to the first, the last, the next, the total, the average or some other filtered or calculated subset.</ns1:p>;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;PAST;previous;An occurrence that occurred or was scheduled to occur in the past. An Act whose effective time is less than 'now'. ('now' is the time the instance is authored.);RECENT;most recent;Restricted to the most recent known occurrence that occurred or was scheduled to occur in the past. The Act with the most recent effective time, still less than 'now'. ('now' is the time the instance is authored.)
v3-ActRelationshipSubset;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipSubset;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipSubset;v3 Code System ActRelationshipSubset;active;False; <ns1:p>Used to indicate that the target of the relationship will be a filtered subset of the total related set of targets.</ns1:p><ns1:p>Used when there is a need to limit the number of components to the first, the last, the next, the total, the average or some other filtered or calculated subset.</ns1:p>;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;_ParticipationSubset;ParticipationSubset;"Used to indicate that the participation is a filtered subset of the total participations of the same type owned by the Act.

                        Used when there is a need to limit the participations to the first, the last, the next or some other filtered subset.";SUM;summary;Represents a 'summary' of all acts that have occurred or were scheduled to occur and which are scheduled to occur in the future. The effectiveTime represents the outer boundary of all occurrences, repeatNumber represents the total number of repetitions, etc.
v3-ActRelationshipSubset;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActRelationshipSubset;2018-08-12;v3.ActRelationshipSubset;v3 Code System ActRelationshipSubset;active;False; <ns1:p>Used to indicate that the target of the relationship will be a filtered subset of the total related set of targets.</ns1:p><ns1:p>Used when there is a need to limit the number of components to the first, the last, the next, the total, the average or some other filtered or calculated subset.</ns1:p>;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;ActRelationshipExpectedSubset;ActRelationshipExpectedSubset;ActRelationshipExpectedSubset;;;
