v3-EntityDeterminer;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EntityDeterminer;2018-08-12;v3.EntityDeterminer;v3 Code System EntityDeterminer;active;False; EntityDeterminer in natural language grammar is the class of words that comprises articles, demonstrative pronouns, and quantifiers. In the RIM, determiner is a structural code in the Entity class to distinguish whether any given Entity object stands for some, any one, or a specific thing.;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;INSTANCE;specific;"Description:A determiner that specifies that the Entity object represents a particular physical thing (as opposed to a universal, kind, or class of physical thing).


                           Discussion: It does not matter whether an INSTANCE still exists as a whole at the point in time (or process) when we mention it, for example, a drug product lot is an INSTANCE even though it has been portioned out for retail purpose.";GROUP;specific group;A determiner that specifies that the Entity object represents a particular collection of physical things (as opposed to a universal, kind, or class of physical thing).  While the collection may resolve to having only a single individual (or even no individuals), the potential should exist for it to cover multiple individuals.
v3-EntityDeterminer;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EntityDeterminer;2018-08-12;v3.EntityDeterminer;v3 Code System EntityDeterminer;active;False; EntityDeterminer in natural language grammar is the class of words that comprises articles, demonstrative pronouns, and quantifiers. In the RIM, determiner is a structural code in the Entity class to distinguish whether any given Entity object stands for some, any one, or a specific thing.;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;KIND;described;Description:A determiner that specifies that the Entity object represents a universal, kind or class of physical thing (as opposed to a particular thing).;GROUPKIND;described group;A determiner that specifies that the Entity object represents a universal, kind or class of collections physical things.  While the collection may resolve to having only a single individual (or even no individuals), the potential should exist for it to cover multiple individuals.
v3-EntityDeterminer;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EntityDeterminer;2018-08-12;v3.EntityDeterminer;v3 Code System EntityDeterminer;active;False; EntityDeterminer in natural language grammar is the class of words that comprises articles, demonstrative pronouns, and quantifiers. In the RIM, determiner is a structural code in the Entity class to distinguish whether any given Entity object stands for some, any one, or a specific thing.;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;KIND;described;Description:A determiner that specifies that the Entity object represents a universal, kind or class of physical thing (as opposed to a particular thing).;QUANTIFIED_KIND;described quantified;The described quantified determiner indicates that the given Entity is taken as a general description of a specific amount of a thing. For example, QUANTIFIED_KIND of syringe (quantity = 3,) stands for exactly three syringes.
