v3-EntityRisk;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EntityRisk;2018-08-12;v3.EntityRisk;v3 Code System EntityRisk;active;False; Kinds of risks associated with the handling of the material..;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;BIO;Biological;The dangers associated with normal biological materials. I.e. potential risk of unknown infections.  Routine biological materials from living subjects.;;;
v3-EntityRisk;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EntityRisk;2018-08-12;v3.EntityRisk;v3 Code System EntityRisk;active;False; Kinds of risks associated with the handling of the material..;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;COR;Corrosive;Material is corrosive and may cause severe injury to skin, mucous membranes and eyes. Avoid any unprotected contact.;;;
v3-EntityRisk;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EntityRisk;2018-08-12;v3.EntityRisk;v3 Code System EntityRisk;active;False; Kinds of risks associated with the handling of the material..;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;ESC;Escape Risk;The entity is at risk for escaping from containment or control.;;;
v3-EntityRisk;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EntityRisk;2018-08-12;v3.EntityRisk;v3 Code System EntityRisk;active;False; Kinds of risks associated with the handling of the material..;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;IFL;inflammable;Material is highly inflammable and in certain mixtures (with air) may lead to explosions.  Keep away from fire, sparks and excessive heat.;EXP;explosive;Material is an explosive mixture.  Keep away from fire, sparks, and heat.
v3-EntityRisk;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EntityRisk;2018-08-12;v3.EntityRisk;v3 Code System EntityRisk;active;False; Kinds of risks associated with the handling of the material..;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;INF;infectious;Material known to be infectious with human pathogenic microorganisms.  Those who handle this material must take precautions for their protection.;BHZ;biohazard;Material contains microorganisms that is an environmental hazard.  Must be handled with special care.
v3-EntityRisk;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EntityRisk;2018-08-12;v3.EntityRisk;v3 Code System EntityRisk;active;False; Kinds of risks associated with the handling of the material..;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;INJ;injury hazard;Material is solid and sharp (e.g., cannulas).  Dispose in hard container.;;;
v3-EntityRisk;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EntityRisk;2018-08-12;v3.EntityRisk;v3 Code System EntityRisk;active;False; Kinds of risks associated with the handling of the material..;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;POI;poison;Material is poisonous to humans and/or animals.  Special care must be taken to avoid incorporation, even of small amounts.;;;
v3-EntityRisk;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EntityRisk;2018-08-12;v3.EntityRisk;v3 Code System EntityRisk;active;False; Kinds of risks associated with the handling of the material..;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;RAD;radioactive;Material is a source for ionizing radiation and must be handled with special care to avoid injury of those who handle it and to avoid environmental hazards.;;;
v3-EntityStatus;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EntityStatus;2018-08-12;v3.EntityStatus;v3 Code System EntityStatus;active;False; Codes representing the defined possible states of an Entity, as defined by the Entity class state machine.;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;normal;normal;"The 'typical' state. Excludes ""nullified"" which represents the termination state of an Entity record instance that was created in error.";active;active;The state representing the fact that the Entity record is currently active.
v3-EntityStatus;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EntityStatus;2018-08-12;v3.EntityStatus;v3 Code System EntityStatus;active;False; Codes representing the defined possible states of an Entity, as defined by the Entity class state machine.;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;normal;normal;"The 'typical' state. Excludes ""nullified"" which represents the termination state of an Entity record instance that was created in error.";inactive;inactive;Definition: The state representing the fact that the entity is inactive.
v3-EntityStatus;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EntityStatus;2018-08-12;v3.EntityStatus;v3 Code System EntityStatus;active;False; Codes representing the defined possible states of an Entity, as defined by the Entity class state machine.;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;normal;normal;"The 'typical' state. Excludes ""nullified"" which represents the termination state of an Entity record instance that was created in error.";terminated;terminated;The state representing the normal termination of an Entity record.
v3-EntityStatus;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EntityStatus;2018-08-12;v3.EntityStatus;v3 Code System EntityStatus;active;False; Codes representing the defined possible states of an Entity, as defined by the Entity class state machine.;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;nullified;nullified;The state representing the termination of an Entity record instance that was created in error.;;;
v3-EquipmentAlertLevel;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EquipmentAlertLevel;2018-08-12;v3.EquipmentAlertLevel;v3 Code System EquipmentAlertLevel;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;C;Critical;Shut Down, Fix Problem and Re-init;;;
v3-EquipmentAlertLevel;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EquipmentAlertLevel;2018-08-12;v3.EquipmentAlertLevel;v3 Code System EquipmentAlertLevel;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;N;Normal;No Corrective Action Needed;;;
v3-EquipmentAlertLevel;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EquipmentAlertLevel;2018-08-12;v3.EquipmentAlertLevel;v3 Code System EquipmentAlertLevel;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;S;Serious;Corrective Action Required;;;
v3-EquipmentAlertLevel;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-EquipmentAlertLevel;2018-08-12;v3.EquipmentAlertLevel;v3 Code System EquipmentAlertLevel;active;False;**** MISSING DEFINITIONS ****;2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;W;Warning;Corrective Action Anticipated;;;
v3-Ethnicity;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-Ethnicity;2018-08-12;v3.Ethnicity;v3 Code System Ethnicity;active;False;" In the United States, federal standards for classifying data on ethnicity determine the categories used by federal agencies and exert a strong influence on categorization by state and local agencies and private sector organizations. The federal standards do not conceptually define ethnicity, and they recognize the absence of an anthropological or scientific basis for ethnicity classification.  Instead, the federal standards acknowledge that ethnicity is a social-political construct in which an individual's own identification with a particular ethnicity is preferred to observer identification.  The standards specify two minimum ethnicity categories: Hispanic or Latino, and Not Hispanic or Latino.  The standards define a Hispanic or Latino as a person of ""Mexican, Puerto Rican, Cuban, South or Central America, or other Spanish culture or origin, regardless of race."" The standards stipulate that ethnicity data need not be limited to the two minimum categories, but any expansion must be collapsible to those categories.  In addition, the standards stipulate that an individual can be Hispanic or Latino or can be Not Hispanic or Latino, but cannot be both.";2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;2135-2;Hispanic or Latino;Hispanic or Latino;2137-8;Spaniard;Spaniard
v3-Ethnicity;http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-Ethnicity;2018-08-12;v3.Ethnicity;v3 Code System Ethnicity;active;False;" In the United States, federal standards for classifying data on ethnicity determine the categories used by federal agencies and exert a strong influence on categorization by state and local agencies and private sector organizations. The federal standards do not conceptually define ethnicity, and they recognize the absence of an anthropological or scientific basis for ethnicity classification.  Instead, the federal standards acknowledge that ethnicity is a social-political construct in which an individual's own identification with a particular ethnicity is preferred to observer identification.  The standards specify two minimum ethnicity categories: Hispanic or Latino, and Not Hispanic or Latino.  The standards define a Hispanic or Latino as a person of ""Mexican, Puerto Rican, Cuban, South or Central America, or other Spanish culture or origin, regardless of race."" The standards stipulate that ethnicity data need not be limited to the two minimum categories, but any expansion must be collapsible to those categories.  In addition, the standards stipulate that an individual can be Hispanic or Latino or can be Not Hispanic or Latino, but cannot be both.";2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;2137-8;Spaniard;Spaniard;2138-6;Andalusian;Andalusian
