Description copied from Concept Domain of same name.  Must be corrected..";2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;_ObservationMeasureScoring;ObservationMeasureScoring;Observation values used to indicate the type of scoring (e.g. proportion, ratio) used by a health quality measure.;PROPOR;proportion measure scoring;A score derived by dividing the number of cases that meet a criterion for quality (the numerator) by the number of eligible cases within a given time frame (the denominator) where the numerator cases are a subset of the denominator cases (e.g., percentage of eligible women with a mammogram performed in the last year).
