Description copied from Concept Domain of same name.  Must be verified.";2018-08-12T00:00:00+10:00;HL7, Inc;complete;_RoleClassMutualRelationship;RoleClassMutualRelationship;A relationship that is based on mutual behavior of the two Entities as being related. The basis of such relationship may be agreements (e.g., spouses, contract parties) or they may be de facto behavior (e.g. friends) or may be an incidental involvement with each other (e.g. parties over a dispute, siblings, children).;SELF;self;"The ""same"" roleclass asserts an identity between playing and scoping entities: that they are in fact instances of the same entity and, in the case of discrepancies (e.g different DOB, gender), that one or both are in error.


                           Usage:


                        playing and scoping entities must have same classcode, but need not have identical attributes or values.


                           Example:


                        a provider registry maintains sets of conflicting demographic data for what is reported to be the same individual."
